"hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:"
34069,"(34069) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Abi Malik, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Muslimama, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: People treat one another with tyranny.
(Abu Ali 873, Bazar 1288)"
34070,"(34070) Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of al-Walid ibn Abi Malik, on the authority of al-Qasim ibn Abd The Most Gracious, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: The man from among them is rewarded against the Muslims.
(Ahmad 1958. Tabarani 7908)"
34071,"(34071) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Hand, on the authority of Abu Mara The servant of Aqeel bin Abi Talib, on the authority of Umm Hani bin Abi Talib, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, conquered In Mecca, two men from my close-in-laws fled to me, so I helped them, or spoke to someone similar to them, and my brother Ali bin Abi came in to meet me. A student, and he said: I will kill them. She said: So I closed the door on them, then I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with the highest He came to Mecca and said: Welcome, and welcome to Umm Hani. What brings you? She said: I said: O Prophet of God, two men from my close-in-laws fled to me, and my brother Ali bin Abi Talib entered upon me and claimed that he He fought them both, and he said: No, we have rewarded whomever you have rewarded, and we have protected whomever you have believed."
34072,"(34072) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Murra, on the authority of Umm Hani’, He said: She told me, she said: Two men from my close-in-laws fled to me on the day of the conquest, so I spared them, then my brother came in and said: I would have killed them, so I closed in on them, then I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Welcome, and welcome, Umm Hani. What brings you? So she told him, and he said: We have rewarded whomever you have rewarded, and we have protected whomever you have believed. She said: I came and prevented you from both of them."
34073,"(34073) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: If The woman is to take authority over the people."
34074,"(34074) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: If The woman is to take charge of the Muslims."
34075,"(34075) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Fudayl bin Zayd al-Raqqashi, and he was During the reign of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, he fought seven battles. He said: Omar sent an army, and I was in that army, so the people of Al-Khattab besieged us. Siriyaj, so when we saw that we would open it from that day, we said: We will go back and have a nap, then we will go and open it, so when When we returned, one of the Muslims’ slaves had lagged behind, so they misled them, so he wrote them a guarantee in a document, then he added it to them. He threw an arrow at them and they left.
 When we returned from the evening, we found them had left. We said to them: What is the matter with you? They said: You have believed in us. We said: We have not done so. Indeed, the one who has believed in you is a servant who has no power over anything. So return so that we may write to Omar. Ibn Al-Khattab, and they said: We do not know your slave from your freedmen. We will not return. If you wish, then kill us, and if you wish, then forgive us. He said: So we wrote to Omar, and Omar wrote: Indeed, Abd al-Muslimeen is one of the Muslims, and I have given him my protection. He said: So Omar permitted Amanah."
34076,"(34076) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The security of women and slaves is permissible."
34077,"(34077) Waki` narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Abi al-Najjoud, on the authority of Zur bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Omar, who said: The woman used to seize upon the Muslims, so her trustworthiness is permissible."
34078,"(34078) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymiyy, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: Muslims are one, the nearest of them strives for it. (Bukhari 3172. 999)"
34079,"(34079) Shababih told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Amr ibn al-Aas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: He rewards some of the Muslims, or he said: A man from among them. (Taalisi 1063. Ahmad 197)"
34080,"(34080) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The protection of the Muslims is one, and the lowest of them will strive with it. (Abu Dawud 5073. Ahmed 398)"
34081,"(34081) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He will punish the Muslims who are the lowest of them. (Abu Dawud 2745, Ahmed 216)"
34082,"(34082) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Atiyya, who said: Omar wrote to the people of Kufa: It was mentioned to me that (matras) in the Persian language means security, so if you say it to someone who does not understand your language, then he is safe."
34083,"(34083) Rayhan bin Saeed told us, he said: Marzuq bin Amr told me, he said: Abu Farqad told me, he said: We were with Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari, on the day we opened the Ahwaz market, a man from the polytheists ran, and two men from the Muslims ran after him, While he was running and they were running, one of them said to him: He is shielded, so the man got up and said: So they took him and brought him, and Abu Musa He beheaded the captives, until it came to the man, and one of them said: This man has been given security, so Abu Musa said: How was security made for him? He said: He was walking across the land, and I said to him: What is a barricade? So he stood up, and Abu Musa said: What is a barricade? He said: Do not be afraid. He said: This is safety. He left the way for him, so we left the way for the man."
34084,"(34084) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Anas, who said: We were besieged in order to cover up, so Al-Hurmuzan descended upon the ruling of Omar. So Abu Musa sent him with me, and when we came to Omar, Al-Hurmuzan was silent and did not speak, so Omar said: Speak, and he said: Living speech. Or the words of a dead person? He said: So he spoke, there is no problem, so he said: We and you Arabs, as long as God leaves us and you, we will kill you. And we excluded you, but since God was with you, we had no relation to you.
 He said: Then Omar said: What do you say, Anas? He said: I said: O Commander of the Faithful, I left behind me a strong thorn, and many people. If I killed him, he would be the most powerful of the people. Life, and it was more severe than their prick, and if she was alive, the greed of the people would please her.
 He said: O Anas, are you ashamed of the killer of Al-Bara’ bin Malik and Majza’ah bin Thawr? When I feared that he would attack him, I said to him: You have no way to kill him. Omar said: Why? Did he give you? Did you catch him? I said: I did not do it, but you said to him: Speak, there is no problem. He said: You must bring someone who will bear witness with you, or I will begin your punishment. He said: So I left him, and behold, Al-Zubair bin Al-Awwam had memorized what I had memorized, so he testified with him, so he left him and embraced Islam. Al-Hurmuzan, and it was made obligatory for him."
34085,"(34085) Waki’ narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: The letter of Omar came to us while we were fighting: When the man said For a man: Do not be fooled, for he has made you safe, and if he says: Do not be afraid, then he has made him safe, and if he says: Mattarah, then he has made him safe, for God knows. Tongues"
34086,"(34086) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Aban bin Salih, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Omar said: If any Muslim man points to an enemy man, “If you go down, I will kill you.” So he went down and thought that he was safe. He believed it"
34087,"(34087) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Talha bin Ubaid Allah bin Kariz, he said: He wrote Omar to the commanders of the soldiers: Any man from among the Muslims referred to a man from the enemy: If you dismount, I will kill you. So he dismounted while he was watching. He is safe, so he has made you safe.
 Buqay bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Shayba told us, he said:"
34088,"(34088) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father; Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent an emir or a convoy to command an army, he would advise him, and he said: If you are besieged, The people of a fortress, and they wanted you to assign to them the protection of God and the protection of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but no You assign to them the protection of God, or the protection of His Messenger, but assign to them your protection and the protection of your fathers, for you are lest you conceal Your blame and the blame of your fathers are too weak for you to hide the pledge of God and the pledge of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace.
 Sufyan said: Alqamiya said: I narrated the hadith of Sulaiman bin Buraidah, Muqatil bin Hayyan, so Muqatil bin Hayyan said: Narrated to us Muslim bin Haysam Al-Abdi, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Muqrin Al-Muzani, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar narration.
(Muslim 4)"
34089,"(34089) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: The letter of Omar came to us while we were in the strife: When You have besieged a palace, and they wanted you to come down to the judgment of God, so do not go down to them, for you do not know what will happen to them. Is it the judgment of God, or not? But send them down to your judgment, then judge them after whatever you wish."
34090,"(34090) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, saying: Shu`abi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Fayd, on the authority of Sulaym ibn Amir, who said: It was There was a covenant between Mu'awiyah and a people of the Romans, so Mu'awiyah went out to walk in their land so that they would break and invade. Upon them, then a man called out in the direction of the army: Loyalty, not treachery, loyalty, not treachery. Then, it was Amr bin Absa. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever has a covenant between him and a people, let him not tighten his contract, nor He will make them lawful, until their time ends, or he will reject them in any case. (Abu Dawud 2753. Tirmidhi 1580)"
34091,"(34091) Muhammad bin Bishr and Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah bin Umar narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When God brings together the ancients and the last on the Day of Resurrection, a banner will be raised for every treacherous person. It was said: This is the treachery of so-and-so, son of so-and-so. (Bukhari 6177, Muslim 1359)"
34092,"(34092) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: For every treacherous person there will be a banner on the Day of Resurrection by which he will be known. (Bukhari 6178 and Muslim 1360)"
34093,"(34093) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Yazid bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abd. God, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Every traitor will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection by which he will be known. It is said: This So-and-so betrayed him. (Muslim 1361)"
34094,"(34094) Affan told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace; In the same way (Bukhari 31861, Muslim 1360)"
34095,"(34095) Hussein bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Abu Nadhri, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; He said: Every traitor will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection, and I betrayed him when he was gone. (Ibn Majah 2873)"
34096,"(34096) Affan narrated to us, he said: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Jaafar, on the authority of Abu Nadhri, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Every traitor will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection. (Muslim 1361. Ahmad 35)"
34097,"(34097) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubayra, on the authority of Ali, he said: For every treacherous person. A banner on the Day of Resurrection."
34098,"(34098) Waki’ narrated to us, Mas’ar narrated to us, he said: I heard his leaders saying in his statement: {Except every ungrateful chosen one}, he said: He who betrays his promise."
34099,"(34099) Affan told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Every traitor has a banner by which he will be known on the Day of Resurrection. (Ahmad 250. Abu Ali 3369)"
34100,"(34100) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid; That Abu Sufyan comforted Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein when they were young.
 He said: And Sufyan said: The security of a minor is not permissible. (Dharmi 2440)"
34101,"(34101) Abd Allah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Ifriqi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not hope to meet the enemy, but ask God for well-being. If you meet them, then stand firm. And remember God, and if they shout or shout, then you must remain silent."
34102,"(34102) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, he said: It was The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, recommended lowering the voice for three times. During fighting, at the Qur’an, and at funerals."
34103,"(34103) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is obligatory to listen and remember when marching. He said: Then he recited: {So be steadfast and remember Allah often}. He said: I said: Should he recite the remembrance loudly? He said: Yes."
34104,"(34104) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Qays ibn Abbad, who said: The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, disliked raising the voice in three situations: during fighting, at funerals, and at funerals. The remembrance"
34105,"(34105) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shuabi narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Al-Mu’ali, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; He disliked raising the voice during fighting, when reciting the Qur’an, and at funerals."
34106,"(34106) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of a man from the people of Medina, on the authority of a writer Abdullah bin Abi Awfa wrote that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not wish to meet the enemy. And ask God for well-being, and when you meet them, and if they come and shout, then you must remain silent. (Ahmed 353 and Abd al-Razzaq 9515)"
34107,"(34107) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Abu Talha’s voice in the army is better than his group. (Ahmad 249. Hakim 352)"
34108,"(34108) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Imran bin Hudayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Majliz; When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would meet an enemy, he would say: O God, you are my support and my helper, I turn to you, and I turn to you. I have roots, and with you I fight."
34109,"(34109) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa saying: He called The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace upon the parties, said: O God, who has sent down the Book, who is quick to judge, who defeats the parties. Defeat them and shake them."
34110,"(34110) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ziyad bin Muslim; A man from the people of India came to the safety of Aden, but a man from the Muslims killed him with his brother. A letter was written about this to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, so he wrote: Do not kill him, and take the blood money from him and send it to his heirs, and he ordered that he be imprisoned."
34111,"(34111) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Habib Al-Muallem, on the authority of Al-Hasan; A man from among the polytheists performed Hajj, and when he returned, a man from among the Muslims met him and killed him, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him to do so. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to give his blood money to his family."
34112,"(34112) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yusuf bin Yaqoub; That a man of the polytheists killed a man of the Muslims, then he entered safely and his brother killed him, so Omar bin Abd killed him. Al-Aziz asked for the blood money, and made it his responsibility in his wealth, and imprisoned him in prison, and sent the blood money to his heirs from among the people of The war"
34113,"(34113) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah (h) and on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; {And if there is a covenant between you and them}, they said: A man is greeted in a place of war, and the man kills him, not The blood money is upon him, and the expiation is upon him."
34114,"(34114) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Issa, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; {And if he is from a people between you and them there is a covenant}, he said: from the people of the covenant, but not a believer."
34115,"(34115) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Ammar bin Ruzaiq, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {And if there is a covenant between a people between you and them}, this is a man who makes covenants, and whose people are family. A covenant, so that his blood money will be handed over to them, and he will free the one who struck him as a slave."
34116,"(34116) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: {And if he is of a people who are enemies to you, and he is a believer}, A man will be killed while his people are polytheists, there will be no covenant between them and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. {Fatahir A believer's slave}, if a Muslim from a polytheist people is killed, and between them and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace A covenant that a faithful slave has made, and he will deliver his blood money to his people who are among them and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings be upon him, a covenant, so his inheritance will be for the Muslims, and his inheritance will be upon them for his polytheist people, who There was a covenant between them and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Muslims would inherit his inheritance, and his inheritance would be For his people because they understand it."
34117,"(34117) Safwan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abi Dhubab, on the authority of Munir bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Dhubab said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I converted to Islam, and I said: O Messenger of God, make For my people what they greeted upon him. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did so. (Abu Ubaid 1487)"
34118,"(34118) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Aban bin Abdullah Al-Bajli narrated to us, he said: Othman bin Abi Hazim narrated to us. On the authority of Sakhr bin Al-Ailah, he said: I took his paternal uncle Al-Maghirah and brought her to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he came. Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about his paternal aunt and told him that she was with him, so the Messenger of God called me. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: He said: O Sakhr, when people embrace Islam, they will keep their money. He said: So We will give it to him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave me water for the children of Salim, so they converted to Islam, so they came to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, so they asked him for water, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Sakhr, when the people embrace Islam, they will achieve Their property and their blood, so he gave it to them, so I paid it to him. (Ibn Saad 31. Dharmi 1473)"
34119,"(34119) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, who said: I asked Ubaid Allah bin Omar about who among his family converted to Islam. Blackness? He said: Whoever of the people of the Sawad embraces Islam from among those who have a responsibilities, he will have his land and his property, and whoever surrenders from among those who have no responsibilities, his property will only be taken. By force, his land is for the Muslims. Ubaidullah said: This is in the book of Omar bin Abdul Aziz."
34120,"(34120) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Whatever city was opened by force, So its people converted to Islam, so they are free, and their property is for the Muslims."
34121,"(34121) Zayd ibn al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Hani ibn Yazid; He mentioned that he was a delegation to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, among his people, and that when the departure of the people to their country came, He gave each man a land in his country wherever he liked."
34122,"(34122) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Whoever converts to Islam will attain He has the right to Islam, his life and his property, except the land, because he has embraced Islam and there is nothing preventing him."
34123,"(34123) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Ghalib al-Abdi, who said: A man from Banu Numayr narrated to me, on the authority of his father. , on the authority of his grandfather, or his paternal grandfather; He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, my people have accepted Islam because I have made such and such for them. Likewise, he said: If you wish, you can return to it, and leaving it is better."
34124,"(34124) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar Al-Birani; Omar bin Abdulaziz said: As for whoever of the people of the earth converts to Islam, he will have the same as his family or wealth as he converted to Islam. His earth is in existence according to what God has bestowed upon the Muslims."
34125,"(34125) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, and Al-Zuhri, who said: It is Sunnah for a man to have what May peace be upon him."
34126,"(34126) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: Al-Akadir gave a jar of manna to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he began to divide it among us. (Ahmed 122)"
34127,"(34127) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; Indeed, I am the one who bestowed a gift to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, even though he was a polytheist, so he accepted it from him."
34128,"(34128) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Abu Salih al-Hanafi, on the authority of Ali; Akkadir Douma gave the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a silk garment, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave it to him. He greeted Ali and said: Spread wine between the women."
34129,"(34129) Muhammad bin Musab told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned a gift from a man of the polytheists. Al-Zuhri said: Then the princes after they accepted Their gifts"
34130,"(34130) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Iyad bin Himar gave a gift to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: O Ayyad, have you converted to Islam? He said: No, so he returned it to him and said: We do not accept the foam of the polytheists.
 Ibn Aoun said: I said to Al-Hasan: What is butter? He said: Al-Rafd. (Abu Dawud 3052. Tirmidhi 1577)"
34131,"(34131) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir; Al-Kalbi brought a cloak and two slippers to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he kissed them and put them on. He even broke them, and the people swear: He does not know if they are smart or not? (Tabarani 4200)"
34132,"(34132) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim; Al-Muqawqis presented a gift to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he accepted it."
34133,"(34133) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Jubayr bin Mutim said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, divided the shares of relatives among the Banu Hashim, and his The request.
(Abu Dawud 2973. Ahmed 18)"
34134,"(34134) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Hashim bin Buraid narrated to us, saying: Husayn bin Maimun narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: I heard Ali saying: I said: O Messenger of God, if... You thought that you should give me our right of the fifth in the Book of God, so divide your life with it, so that no one will dispute with me after you. He said: So he did that. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, brought him to me, and I apportioned it to him as the life of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. Then Abu Bakr cursed him, so I divided him with the life of Abu Bakr. Then Omar cursed him, so I divided him with the life of Omar.
 Until it was the last year of Omar, a lot of money came to him, so he isolated our share, then sent it to me and said: This Your right, then take it and divide it where you used to divide it. So I said: O Commander of the Faithful, the year has spared us. And among the Muslims, a pilgrim came to him, and he responded to him that year, and then no one called us to him after Omar, until I This is my place, so I met Al-Abbas after I left Omar’s house, and he said: O Ali, you have deprived us of lunch, something that will not be returned to us. Never until the Day of Resurrection, and he was a shrewd man. (Abu Dawud 2976; Abu Ali 359)"
34135,"(34135) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of al-Zuhri, and Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of Yazid. Bin Hurmuz; Indeed, Najd wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him about the shares of relatives, who is it for? So he wrote: You wrote to ask me about the shares of a relative, who does it belong to? So he is for us. He said: Omar ibn al-Khattab called on us to marry the most faithful man of ours, to serve our breadwinner from him, and to pay off his debts. He was in debt to us, so we refused to do so unless he handed it over to us all, which he refused to do, so we left it to him."
34136,"(34136) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Al-Hanafiyyah, he said: After the death of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, people disagreed about these two arrows. The arrow of the Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the arrow of his relatives. Ta’ifa said: The arrow of the Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. For the caliph after him, and a group said: The share of relatives is for the relatives of the caliph, so they agreed to make These two arrows are in the horseshoes and in the equipment in the path of God."
34137,"(34137) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib; When Omar bin Abdul Aziz rose, he was sent with these two arrows: the arrow of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the arrow A relative, meaning the descendants of Hashim."
34138,"(34138) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Sadi; {By the one who is close}, he said: They are the sons of Abdul-Muttalib."
34139,"(34139) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, who said: He wrote “Najdi” to Ibn Abbas. He asks him about the shares of a relative? So Ibn Abbas wrote to him: We were claiming that we were them, but our people refused to do that to us."
34140,"(34140) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Hasan; In these verses: {For Allah, and for the Messenger, and for his relatives, and the orphans, and the needy, and the wayfarer}, He said: He did not give his family House after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The five were Abu Bakr, Omar, and no one else, and they believed that That to the Imam, he will place it in the way of God, and for the poor wherever God has shown it."
34141,"(34141) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: A man came To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, I pledge allegiance to you for jihad. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Peace and blessings be upon him: Do you have a father? He said: Yes, he said: Go and fight against him, for he is a good fighter. (Ibn Hibban 419)"
34142,"(34142) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar and Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abu Abbas. Al-Makki, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: A man came to ask the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, permission to perform jihad, and he said The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: He revived your parents. He said: Yes. He said: So he struggled with them. (Bukhari 3004, Muslim 1975)"
34143,"(34143) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Kurayb, who said: A woman came to Ibn Abbas. And her son wanted to invade and his mother hated him, so Ibn Abbas said to him: Obey your mother and sit with her."
34144,"(34144) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, who said: A man came to Ibn Abbas. He said: I wanted to invade, but my parents forbid me? He said: Obey your parents and sit down, for the Romans will find someone to invade them other than you."
34145,"(34145) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha, on the authority of his father Talha bin Muawiyah Al-Salami, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said, O Messenger of God, I want to wage jihad with you. For the sake of God, I seek the face of God by this. He said: Is your mother alive? I said: Yes. He said: Hold on to it. I said: I do not see the understanding of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on his authority. So I repeated it to him several times, and he said: Stick to her feet and then you will go to Paradise."
34146,"(34146) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; Two men left their father, an old man, and went on a campaign. At the age of that age, he sent them back to their father and said: No. You will separate from him until he dies."
34147,"(34147) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Yazid; A man asked Ubaid bin Umayr: Should a man fight while his parents are haters, or one of them? He said: No."
34148,"(34148) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Salim, or Abdullah bin Utba. Muhammad ibn Talha wanted to invade, so his mother went to Omar, so he ordered him to stay. When Uthman took charge, he wanted to invade, so his mother came. Othman, so he ordered him to stand, and he said: Omar did not force me, or insist on me, so he said: But I will force you."
34149,"(34149) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Ma’n ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: A man invaded towards the Levant, and he was called : Shaiban, and he has an old father, so his father said poetry about that:
What makes you realize that the Lord of the night has darkened you, and darkness is beloved?
Have you neglected me so that when you leave me, I see the person as two people, and he is close?
Shayban, if the armies depart, you will find them suffering for days in which there are engagements.
 He said: That happened to Omar, so he turned it away"
34150,"(34150) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If your mother gives you permission to wage jihad And you know that you have a desire to sit, so sit."
34151,"(34151) Waki’ told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jahadi, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: A man came to the Prophet and prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. He asked for your permission in jihad, so he said: Do you have anything to do with Jihad? He said: Yes, he said: Sit with her.
(Abdul Razzaq 9286)"
34152,"(34152) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a servant fights over a horse His master, so it was divided among the Muslims. It was divided into his master’s horses, just as it was divided into the Muslims’ horses, so it was the property of his master, and it was divided. It is given to a slave just as it is given to a Muslim man."
34153,"(34153) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman; Omar granted the people of Sawad three days of hospitality for the wayfarer."
34154,"(34154) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shuabi narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla; Omar bin Al-Khattab stipulated that the people of Sawad should receive hospitality for a day and a night, and one of them used to say: Shabaa, Shabaa. It means night."
34155,"(34155) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawwi narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of al-Ahnaf ibn Qays; Omar stipulated that they be given hospitality for a day and a night, and that they repair the bridges, even if a Muslim man is killed on their land. May his death be upon you."
34156,"(34156) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah ibn Mudharib al-Abdi, on the authority of Omar; He stipulated that the people of the month should receive hospitality for a day and a night, so if rain or sickness detains them, then two days. They stayed longer than that, spent of their money, and were only assigned what they could afford."
34157,"(34157) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Hospitality is for three days, and whatever comes after that is charity. (Abu Dawud 3743. Ahmed 288)"
34158,"(34158) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Shurayh Al-Khuza’i, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him honor his guests, his reward. Day and night, and it is not permissible for a guest to stay with his friend until he embarrasses him. Hospitality is three, and whatever he spends Ali after three days, so he has spoken the truth.
(Bukhari 6019 and Muslim 1352)"
34159,"(34159) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Wahhab, on the authority of a man from the Ansar; Among the things that Omar imposed on the people of Dhimma was hospitality for a day and a night."
34160,"(34160) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Ibn Suraqi told me; That Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah wrote to the people of Deir Tayaa: You must stay the guest for three days, and if you take our responsibility Innocent from the horrors of the army."
34161,"(34161) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: Al-Dhiyafah is three. days, and what comes after that is truth. (Ahmed 7. Abdul Razzaq 20528)"
34162,"(34162) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Ibn Umar camped with a people, and when three days had passed, he said: Oh Beneficial, spend on us, for we have no need for it to be given in charity."
34163,"(34163) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Ayman, who said: Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ali used to come down to On us, and if we spend on him for three days, he refuses to accept it from us."
34164,"(34164) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The traveler has three A number of days for whoever passes through it, and whatever he passes is a charity, and every good deed is a charity."
34165,"(34165) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: The guest’s right is for three days, but it was not permissible. That is the truth."
34166,"(34166) Waki’ told us, he said: Shuabi told us, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juniy, he said: I heard Jundub al-Bajlili, He says: We were a share of their food without sharing their homes with them, and we would take medicine and he would direct us from the village. To the village."
34167,"(34167) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Waqa’ al-Asadi, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, who said: We were with Salman al-Farisi in Ghazaa, either in Jalula’ah, or in Nawand, he said: A man passed by who had gathered some fruit, so he said: So he divided it among His companions, then Salman passed by and insulted him. He replied to Salman, and he did not know him. He said: Then he was told: This is Salman. So he returned to Salman. He apologized to him, and the man said to him: What is permissible for non-Muslims, O Abu Abdullah? He said: Three: from your blindness to guidance, and from your poverty to your wealth, and when you accompany a companion among them, you eat of his food. He may eat of your food, and you may ride his animal, and do not turn him away from where he wants."
34168,"(34168) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: Horses are tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection. (Muslim 1493. Ahmad 112)"
34169,"(34169) Abdullah bin Idris and Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Urwa Al-Bariqi, He raised him up and said: Goodness is held in the horses’ forelocks until the Day of Resurrection: reward and spoils. Ibn Idris added in his hadith: Camels are the strength of their owners, and sheep are their blessings. (Muslim 1493. Tabarani 399)"
34170,"(34170) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Urwah Al-Bariqi, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Horses have goodness tied by their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection, reward. And the spoils.
(Nasa’i 4418 and Ahmad 376)"
34171,"(34171) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Zur’i bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Jarir, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, twisting the forelock of his horse with his finger, and saying: Goodness is held in the horses' horseshoes until the Day of Resurrection, the reward and the spoils. (Muslim 1493. Ahmad 361)"
34172,"(34172) Shababih told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Horses will have their goodness tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection. (Ahmed 455)"
34173,"(34173) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: Blessing is in the forelocks of horses. (Bukhari 2851, Muslim 1494)"
34174,"(34174) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Sa’id al-Bazzar, on the authority of Makhoul, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Horses will be tied with goodness by their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection, and their family will help them.
(Saeed bin Mansour 2429)"
34175,"(34175) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Shabib bin Gharqadiya, on the authority of Urwah Al-Bariqi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Goodness is bound by the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection. (Bukhari 3443, Muslim 1494)"
34176,"(34176) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, he said: Whoever is associated A horse for the sake of God whose dung, and urine, and fodder, and such and such, will be in its balance on the Day of Resurrection. (Abu Awan 7386)"
34177,"(34177) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid bin Bahram narrated to us, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Asma’ Bint Zaid, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever mates a horse in the path of God, then spends on it in the hope of seeking His fullness, his hunger, his thirst, his thirst, his dung, and his urine will be in the scales of the Day of Resurrection, and whoever is associated with A horse, hypocrisy, and reputation - that will be a loss in his balance on the Day of Resurrection."
34178,"(34178) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, on the authority of a man from Al-Ansar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: There are three types of horses: a horse that a man rides in the path of God. Its price is a reward, a reward for riding it, a reward for a naked animal, a reward for its fodder, and a horse that a man can lock up and bet on. On him, his price is a burden, his fodder is a burden, his riding is a burden, and a horse is a burden, so perhaps they will be a ward off poverty if God willing (Ahmed 395)"
34179,"(34179) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Mas’udi told us, on the authority of Muzahim ibn Zufar al-Taymi, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Khabbab, who said: Horses Three: a horse for God, a horse for you, and a horse for Satan. As for the horse that belongs to him: it is the horse that is fought against, and as for the horse that is yours: it is the horse that the man steals away. As for the horse that belongs to Satan: it was not attacked and shown to him.
(Tabarani 3707)"
34180,"(34180) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba bin Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah; {And prepare for them what you are able} He said: fortresses. He said: {And of the tether of horses} He said: females."
34181,"(34181) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Suleiman bin Bilal narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father. Huraira, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The horses will be tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection. Resurrection
(Bukhari 2371, Muslim 282)"
34182,"(34182) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Malik bin Anas told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Abbad Bin Tamim, on the authority of Abu Bashir Al-Ansari, who said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on some of his travels, so he sent Messenger: Do not leave a string necklace on the neck of a camel unless it is cut off. (Bukhari 35051 Muslim 1672)"
34183,"(34183) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Sa’id al-Bazzar, on the authority of Makhoul, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Imitate them, but do not imitate them the strings, meaning horses. (Saeed bin Mansour 2429)"
34184,"(34184) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Yazeed bin Jabir told us, he said: Al-Qasim told me, on the authority of my father In front of him, he said: Imitate them, but do not imitate the strings, meaning horses."
34185,"(34185) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: Imitate horses, but do not imitate strings."
34186,"(34186) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Mundakir, on the authority of Rabi’ah ibn Abdullah ibn Al-Hudair, he said: Whenever Omar was riding on a horse or a camel in the path of God, he said: When he passed Wadi al-Qura, or The same way as Egypt, so do with it as you wish."
34187,"(34187) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: When Ibn Umar was carrying a camel on a For the sake of God, he stipulated that his companion would not destroy him until he reached Wadi al-Qura, or his shoes from the road to Egypt. If he does not do that, then he is free of all his wealth and can do whatever he wants."
34188,"(34188) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; He was asked about a man who gives something for the sake of God. What does he do with what he has left? He said: When he reaches the beginning of his purpose, then it is the fullness of his wealth, and he will do with it what he used to do with his wealth."
34189,"(34189) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Umar Mawla Ghufari, who said: I wanted to invade, so I prepared with what I had on hand, and he sent I came to a man who helped me with sixty dinars in the name of God. He said: So I went to Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab and mentioned that to him, and I said: Should I pray for my family in proportion to what I spent? He said: No, but when you reach the beginning of the matter, then it is the same as your master. Then you came to Al-Qasim bin Muhammad and mentioned that to him. He said to me the same as what Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said."
34190,"(34190) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab; Concerning a man who is given something for the sake of God and the thing remains with him. He said: Whatever is left over is his."
34191,"(34191) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, and Ata’; Concerning a man who is given something for the sake of God, and some of it is left over, so they said: It is for him."
34192,"(34192) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: He makes it in Like him"
34193,"(34193) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, who said: I heard a sheikh in the prayer place, saying: Abu Hurairah said: If you want to wage jihad, do not ask people. If you are given something, make it like it."
34194,"(34194) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who is given something for the sake of God, and something is left over from it. He said: He makes it something like it."
34195,"(34195) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who is given something for the sake of God, and he keeps the thing with him, he said: He makes it like it."
34196,"(34196) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He will go on those paths."
34197,"(34197) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Wasil bin Abi Jamil Abi Bakr, on the authority of Mujahid, he said : What about a caged animal that is with a man and gets stuck, so he sells it and increases its price? He said: Whatever he adds, he is locked up with her."
34198,"(34198) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a she-camel is imprisoned for the sake of God, her calves With her status."
34199,"(34199) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Suleiman ibn Musa; In the imam when he turns? He said: The knight is written as a knight, and the footman is written as a footman."
34200,"(34200) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Abu Hurriyah, who said: Al-Hasan was asked about the people who were in a campaign, So they take the medicine and make fun of it, and he shows them the nakedness of the enemy? Al-Hasan said: He used to do that."
34201,"(34201) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Shu`abi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juniy, he said: I heard Jundub al-Bajlili, He says: We used to take medicine and he would guide us from village to village."
34202,"(34202) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Abu Hurri, on the authority of al-Hasan; In the case of a man whose wife was taken captive and her husband ransomed her from the enemy, who would be his female slave? He said: No."
34203,"(34203) Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: There are free women who were captured by the enemy, so he bought them. A man, will it happen to them? He said: No, nor will they enslave them, but they will give them themselves for what He took them with, and nothing more than that."
34204,"(34204) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Masawar Al-Warraq, who said: I asked Al-Sha’bi about a woman from among the people of the people of Dhimma who had been taken captive. The enemy, then the Muslims attacked her, and she fell into the arrows of one of them? He said: It will be returned to the people of its covenant."
34205,"(34205) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the people of Dhimma, the enemy will take them captive, then the Muslims will attack them. He said: They will not be enslaved."
34206,"(34206) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, he said: People of the non-Muslim religion will not be sold."
34207,"(34207) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, he said: Free people are not sold."
34208,"(34208) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ibn Awn narrated to us, on the authority of Ghadhirith al-Anbari, he said: We came to Omar, and Ibn Awn said: Either he said about women, or he said: about female slaves who used to help during the pre-Islamic era, so he commanded their children to stand up to him. Their fathers, and that they should not be enslaved."
34209,"(34209) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the enemy captured a Muslim man, and a merchant bought him He sought the merchant until he returned what he had bought for him, and if they captured a Muslim property and a merchant bought it, then His master found it, so he has more right to its price. And if they buy from a non-Muslim, he should go to the merchant until he pays it. God is its price."
34210,"(34210) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ said: In the heat, the enemy takes him captive, then The Muslim buys them, as is said about women, and Amr bin Dinar said the same, meaning he gives them themselves. For the price he took them for."
34211,"(34211) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Abu Muadh, on the authority of Abu Hariz; He heard Al-Sha'bi saying: Whatever captives are in the hands of the merchants, the free person cannot be sold, so return to the merchant his head. What's wrong?"
34212,"(34212) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Salem ibn Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: It was Ali A man was burdened by the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and it was said to him: He suffered a burden, and he died. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he was in Hell, so they went to look and found a cloak on him that he had tied up. (Bukhari 3074, Ibn Majah 2829)"
34213,"(34213) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Abi Your age; He heard Zayd bin Khalid Al-Janni narrating: A man from among the Muslims died at the news of Khaybar, and that he was mentioned to the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave his command, and he said: Bless your companion, and the faces of the people changed because of that, and when he saw that He said: He committed injustice in the path of God. We searched his belongings and found Jewish beads worth two dirhams.
(Abu Dawud 2703, Malak 458)"
34214,"(34214) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, On the authority of Abu Amrah, on the authority of Zaid bin Khaled, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Like him"
34215,"(34215) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Hakam bin Atiyya narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Mukhays Al-Yashkari, he said: I heard Anas Ibn Malik, he said: It was said: O Messenger of God, so-and-so, your servant, was martyred. He said: No, I saw a cloak on him. Expensive
(Ahmed 180)"
34216,"(34216) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rose among us and gave a sermon. He mentioned the deception, and he venerated him and magnified his affairs. Then he said: O people! I will never find that any of you will come on the Day of Resurrection with a camel with sticks on his neck, saying: O Messenger of God, Help me, and I will say: I have no authority over you, I have conveyed the message to you, and I will never meet any of you who will come upon me on the Day of Resurrection. I saw a cow that was mooing. He said: O Messenger of God, help me. Then I said: I have no power over you. I have conveyed the message to you. Nor Have you ever found that one of you will come on the Day of Resurrection with a horse with a blood clot on his neck, saying: O Messenger of God, help me. So I say: I have no power over you, I have conveyed the message to you, and I will never see one of you come on the Day of Resurrection with a fasting on his neck. He says: O Messenger of God, help me, and I say: I do not possess anything for you, I have conveyed the message to you, nor will any of you come to me. On the Day of Resurrection, there will be upon his neck a soul who has cried out, and he will say: O Messenger of God, help me, and I will say: I have no power over you. Something, I have conveyed to you. (Bukhari 3073, Muslim 1462)"
34217,"(34217) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Sulayman bin Buraydah, on the authority of My father, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would send an emir to command a convoy or an army, he would say: Do not go to extremes."
34218,"(34218) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; Abu Hamid Al-Sa’idi, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the brother of Banu Sa’id, told him: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told him: May God bless him and grant him peace. He used Ibn Al-Lutbiyah and said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, none of you should take anything from it. Without his right, unless he comes to God carrying him on the Day of Resurrection, I do not know of anyone who came to God carrying a camel that was smelly. Or cows mooing, or sheep bleating, then he raised his hand until I could see the white of his armpits, then he said: Oh God, have I conveyed the message? Abu Hamid said: My eyes have seen and my ears have heard. (Muslim 1464)"
34219,"(34219) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Abu Hamid Al-Sa’idi, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace; In a similar way, except that he said: the cover of your armpits. (Bukhari 2597, Muslim 1463)"
34220,"(34220) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Adiy bin Umairah Al-Kindi said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O people, whoever among you works for us He worked, so We concealed a secret, and what is above it is a deceit that will be brought with it on the Day of Resurrection. He said: Then a man from the Ansar rose up to him. Black as if I could see him. He said: Accept your deeds from me, O Messenger of God. He said: What is that? He said: I heard you saying what you said: He said: And I say it now: Whoever We appoint to do a job, let him bring us a little and a lot. Whatever he was given, he took, and whatever he was prohibited from, he withheld."
34221,"(34221) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Adiy bin Umayrah Al-Kindi. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he mentioned something similar to it, except that he said: He is a deceit, and he will bring it to you. On the Day of Resurrection"
34222,"(34222) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In his saying {And whatever the Messenger has given you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, abstain from it}, he said: He used to give you spoils, And he forbade them from deception. (Tiberius 28)"
34223,"(34223) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid ibn Khusaifi, on the authority of Salem, an obedient servant, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Rifa’a gave a boy to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he went out with him to He was informed, and he descended between the afternoon and the sunset, and a flying arrow struck the boy and killed him, so we said: Congratulations to you in Paradise, and he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, your veil will now be burned in the fire. A group of Muslims boiled over, so a man from the Ansar said: Oh. Messenger of God, I was struck with two traps on that day. He said: An equal share of the fire of Hell will be given to you. (Ibn Hibban 4852 Hakim 40)"
34224,"(34224) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who disperses and the army disperses, he said: He will give him in charity on behalf of that army."
34225,"(34225) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of al-Muthanna, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: If the deceit is found in a man He was taken, flogged, his head and beard were shaved, and everything he had on his journey except animals was taken and burned. He departed, and he never took an arrow from the Muslims. He said: And I was informed that Abu Bakr and Omar used to do it."
34226,"(34226) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning ghoul, it is found among a man. He said: He burns his saddlebags."
34227,"(34227) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Huraim told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amr bin Salem, he said: Our companions were They say: The punishment for the one who commits fraud is to burn his tent and his belongings."
34228,"(34228) Dawud bin Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Muhammad bin Zaydah, on the authority of Salem Bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar Bin Al-Khattab; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever you find has committed adultery, burn his belongings."
34229,"(34229) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ammar al-Dhani, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He wrote to a man from the People of the Book: Peace be upon you."
34230,"(34230) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I asked Abraham, and Mujahid, how is it written to? People of the Dhim? Mujahid said: It is written: Peace be upon whoever follows guidance, and he said: Abraham said: Peace be upon you."
34231,"(34231) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Amr bin Uthman, on the authority of Abu Burda, who said: I heard him say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote May God bless him and grant him peace to a man from the People of the Book. You are a Muslim. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had not finished his letter until a letter from that man came to him to read. Peace be upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, replied at the bottom of his book."
34232,"(34232) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Khalid bin Salamah, on the authority of Amer, he said: Khalid bin wrote Al-Walid from Al-Hira to the Persian satraps: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, from Khalid bin Al-Walid to the Persian satraps, peace. On the one who follows the guidance."
34233,"(34233) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, he said: I heard Ayyad al-Ash’ari, he said: I witnessed the Yarmouk, he said: Then Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah said: Who will bet on me? He said: Then a young man said: I do, if you are not angry. He said: Then he preceded him. He said: I saw the two thorns of Abu Ubaidah jumping, and he He succeeded him on an Arab mare. (Bayhaqi 21)"
34234,"(34234) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: They were making bets on the covenant of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. Al-Zuhri said: The first person to give it to him was Omar bin Al-Khattab. (Abdul Razzaq 9693)"
34235,"(34235) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Al-Alqamah had a bardun that he used to bet on."
34236,"(34236) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; Alqamah raced against a man and overtook him, so he took hold of his bridle."
34237,"(34237) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: There is no problem with proof. If a horse has a freed horse, if it outpaces it has a head start, and if it does not outpace then there is nothing wrong with it. (Malik 468)"
34238,"(34238) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever enters a horse between two horses and is sure that it will race It is gambling, and whoever puts a horse between two horses and is not sure of being ahead of him is not gambling. (Abu Dawud 2572 and Ibn Majah 2876)"
34239,"(34239) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abdullah bin Husayn Al-Ajli: Hudhayf preceded the people on a gray-haired horse. He said: So I entered upon him while he was sitting on his feet, his buttocks not touching the ground. He was happy with him, dripping with sweat, and his horse was on his trough, and he was sitting and looking at him, and people were entering upon him."
34240,"(34240) Waki` narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abu Salama; Hudhaifa preceded the people in his bardhun."
34241,"(34241) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; Omar Ibn Al-Khattab was the best horse racer and raced."
34242,"(34242) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: They used to outpace the horses. And the stirrups, and on their feet."
34243,"(34243) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God included God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to send the horses that had been gathered from among the guards to the farewell gatherings, and the ones that did not It goes from the end of farewell to the mosque of Banu Zurayq. (Muslim 1492. Abu Dawud 2568)"
34244,"(34244) Zayd ibn Harun told us, saying: Sa’id ibn Zayd informed us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr ibn Khairit, on the authority of Abu Labid, he said: The horses were sent, and Al-Hakam bin Ayyub was on Basra, he said: So we went out to look at it, so we said: If only We went to Anas bin Malik, so we went to him while he was in his palace in the corner, so we said to him: O Abu Hamza, Were they betting on the covenant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, by God, he will see it, meaning the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a horse of his own, to which it will be said: Glory be to Him. She came earlier, so he was surprised by that. (Ahmad 1600 Darami 2430)"
34245,"(34245) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, who said: Two men saw a gazelle while they were in ihram. So they confronted him and he saw us, and he threw a stick at him and broke it, so Omar came and Ibn Awf was beside him, and he said to Abd al-Rahman: What? You say? He said: This is gambling, even if it was a race."
34246,"(34246) Hafs told us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saddled the horses, and placed a shield between them: paper holders, and saddled the camels, and did not He mentions the precedence."
34247,"(34247) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Hudhayf. Ibn Al-Yaman in Al-Mada'in is pulling between the two targets in a shirt."
34248,"(34248) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Abi Nafi’, the client of Abu Ahmad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no precedence except in a shoe, or a hoof, or a blade. (Tirmidhi) 1700. Ahmed 474)"
34249,"(34249) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abu al-Fawares, on the authority of Abu Hurairah He said: There is no precedence except in a shoe or a shoe."
34250,"(34250) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid, saying: I saw Ibn Umar squeezing between the two targets in A shirt, and he says: I am in it, I am in it, meaning when he is right, then he returns, shouldering his bow, until he passes through the market."
34251,"(34251) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I asked him about being ahead in the battlefield? He saw no harm in it."
34252,"(34252) Waki’ told us, he said: Nafi’ bin Omar told us, he said: I asked Amr bin Dinar about being ahead? He said: Eat and feed me."
34253,"(34253) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: The angels do not bring anything from you, except bets and arrows. (Saeed bin Mansour 2453)"
34254,"(34254) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man from Muzainah, or Jahinah, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, heard a people saying in their slogans: O forbidden, so he said: O permissible. (Ahmad 471, Hakim 108)"
34255,"(34255) Waki’ told us, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Iyas bin Salamah, on the authority of his father, he said: We fought with Abi Bakr and Hawazin, so our motto was: Die, die."
34256,"(34256) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Al-Umays told us, on the authority of Iyas bin Salamah, on the authority of his father, he said: Our motto was with Khaled bin Al-Walid: I died, I died. (Abu Awan 7546)"
34257,"(34257) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, he said: It was the slogan of the Muslims on the Day of Resurrection. Muslim: O Companions of Surah Al-Baqarah."
34258,"(34258) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Malik narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif al-Yami, who said: When the Muslims were defeated on the day of Hunayn They were called: O Companions of Surah Al-Baqarah, so they returned and they had Hunayn, which means weeping. (Muslim 761 Abdul Razzaq 9465)"
34259,"(34259) Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Ghalib bin Suleiman Abu Salih told us, he said: Al-Zubayr bin Sarakh told us, he said: Musaab bin Al-Zubayr said to us, and we are the companions of Al-Mukhtar: Let your motto be: They will not be helped, for this was the motto of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace."
34260,"(34260) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: It was a slogan The Ansar: Abdullah, and the motto of the Emigrants: Abdul Rahman."
34261,"(34261) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: You will meet the enemy tomorrow, and your motto is: They will not help you. (Nasa’i 10451. Ahmad 65)"
34262,"(34262) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Talha a concubine of ten, and he said: Your motto is: Oh ten. (Ibn Saad 219)"
34263,"(34263) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of al-Nu’man bin Sa’d, who said: I heard Al-Mughirah bin Shu`ba, he says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The motto of the Muslims on the Day of Resurrection on the Path: O God, grant us peace. Say hello (Tirmidhi 2432, Ibn Aden 1631)"
34264,"(34264) Zaid told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: It was The motto of the Muhajireen is: Abdullah, and the motto of the Ansar is: Abd al-Rahman. (Abu Dawud 2588)"
34265,"(34265) Hussein bin Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Husayn, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Uqba, on the authority of Abu Uqba, who was a freedman from the people of Persia, he said: I witnessed with the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the day of Uhud, I hit a man from the polytheists, so I said: Take it from me while I am the Persian boy. So she reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: No, you said: Take it from me while I am the Ansar boy.
(Abu Dawud 5082, Ahmed 295)"
34266,"(34266) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Hisham bin Saad told us, he said: Qais bin Bashir al-Taghlabi told me, He said: My father was a companion of Abu Darda’ in Damascus, and he was in Damascus a man from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. It was said to him: Ibn al-Handhaliyah, from the Ansar. He passed by us one day while we were with Abu al-Darda’, and Abu al-Darda’ said: Speak to us that will benefit us and will not harm you. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent two convoys, and she came and a man from among them came and sat down. In the gathering in which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was present, he said to a man beside him: If you had seen us when we met The enemy carried someone so-and-so and was stabbed, so he said: Take her, and I am the forgiving boy. So he said: I do not see him except that his reward has been annulled. So he said: I do not see it. That is a force. He said: They disputed over it and disagreed until the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard that and said: Glory be to God, no. It is great that he should be rewarded and praised, so I saw Abu Al-Darda’ being pleased with that until he was raised, until I saw that he would bless him. Knees, and he says: Did you hear it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? And he says: Yes.
(Abu Dawud 4086. Ahmad 179)"
34267,"(34267) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, or others, who said: You did not want to You will hear on the Day of Al-Qadisiyah: I am the young man Al-Nakha’i, except you heard him."
34268,"(34268) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, he said: Amr was Ibn Maadi was in distress. He passed by us on the Day of Qadisiyah while we were in ranks. He said: O Arabs, be a mighty lion. The lion is the one who is most prosperous, and the Persian is the he-goat after it has met its meteorite."
34269,"(34269) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of Hunayn:
 I am the Prophet, there is no lie, I am the son of Abdul Muttalib."
34270,"(34270) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: It was a she-camel of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. It was called Al-'Adhabay' and it was not preceded by a greeting, so a Bedouin came sitting next to him and he preceded her. This was difficult for the Muslims, so when The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw what was on their faces. They said: O Messenger of God, the lions ran ahead of them. The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: It is God’s right not to raise anything in this world except His status.
(Bukhari 2871, Abu Dawud 4769)"
34271,"(34271) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a similar manner. (Bukhari 6501 and Ibn Hibban 703)"
34272,"(34272) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drove the camels, but he did not mention racing."
34273,"(34273) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Saad bin Saeed, he said: I heard Ali bin Al-Hussein say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is among us. May God bless him and grant him peace. In the invasion of Tabuk, the Ansar said: The race, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The race, if you wish."
34274,"(34274) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: A man narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: We went out with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a journey, so we stayed at a certain place, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Come until I will race against you. She said: So I raced against him, so I raced against him, and after that I went out with him on another journey, so we went down to another place, and he said: Come until I will race against you. She said: He raced against me. He struck me between my shoulders and said: This is the case with you. (Nasa’i 8943. Tabarani 124)"
34275,"(34275) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman, he said: I went out with my father to Al-Jabban, and he said to him: Come O my son, until I race with you. He said: So I raced with him and he raced with me."
34276,"(34276) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, preceded me, and I preceded him. Hammad said: Al-Hadhar."
34277,"(34277) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: They used to stay on their feet."
34278,"(34278) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Yazid Al-Dhuli, he said: I said to Sa’id Ibn Al-Musayyab: What do you say about getting ahead of yourself by throwing stones? He said: There is no harm in it."
34279,"(34279) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Nafi’ bin Omar narrated to us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah; About a man who says: I will compete with you on the condition that you respond to me: his thought."
34280,"(34280) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated to say: I will race with you on the condition that you will race against me."
34281,"(34281) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They hated for anyone of them to say To his companion: I race against you on the condition that you race against me, so if I race against you then it is mine, otherwise it is on you, and it is gambling."
34282,"(34282) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Aasam; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled that if a slave leaves the house of war before his master, then he is free. His master after him did not return it to him, and if the master left before the slave from the house of war, and then the slave left after him, he would return it to him. Her master"
34283,"(34283) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Muqassam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to free the slaves who came to him before their masters, when they converted to Islam, and he freed On the Day of Taif, two legs.
(Ahmad 2230 Darami 2508)"
34284,"(34284) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: When a man came from the enemy If a Muslim accepts his wealth, then his wealth comes to him after him, he has more right to it, and if his wealth comes before him, he is free."
34285,"(34285) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Muslims saw no harm in what ??He was brought back from the enemy’s land, of what there is no price there."
34286,"(34286) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ziyad bin Anam, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Imran, who said: I heard Al-Qasim and Salim saying: You did not cut down any of the trees of the enemy’s land to make a stake, or a club, or a cross, or a plank. Or a mug, or a door, there is no problem with it, but whatever is found for him to be made of that, give it to the spoils."
34287,"(34287) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, and Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Sha’ithi, on the authority of Makhoul, he said: Whatever you cut off from the enemy’s land and make from it a bowl, or a stake, or a crowbar, or a peg, there is no problem with it, and there is no problem with it. I found some of that to be done and it led him to the spoils."
34288,"(34288) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Hassan, who said: I approached Medina, and behold, the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him on the pulpit, and Bilal was standing before him, holding a sword, and when I saw black banners, I said: Who? This? They said: Amr bin Al-Aas came from your army. (Tirmidhi 3274 and Ibn Majah 2816)"
34289,"(34289) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Amra, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a black cloak belonging to Aisha Marhal. (Tirmidhi 1481, Ibn Majah 2818)"
34290,"(34290) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abul-Fadl, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: It was the opinion of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. It is called the punishment. (Ibn Saad 455)"
34291,"(34291) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Harith bin Makhshi, who said: His opinion was Ali. Black, and those camels saw it."
34292,"(34292) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Harith bin Makhshi; The vision of Ali was black on the day of the camel, and the vision of Al-Zubayr and the camel was black."
34293,"(34293) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Usama bin Zayd narrated to us, saying: Our sheikhs narrated to us; That Khalid bin Al-Walid’s vision was black on the day of Damascus."
34294,"(34294) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hasan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Adiy bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, He said: I met my uncle and he had the flag, so I said to him: Where do you want to go? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to go to a man who married his father’s wife after him, so that I could kill him, or I behead him."
34295,"(34295) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a marriage contract with Amr bin Al-Aas. (Abdul Razzaq 9641)"
34296,"(34296) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit; That Abu Bakr said to Khalid bin Al-Walid: Bring me your spear. So he gathered a banner for him, then said to him: March, for God With you"
34297,"(34297) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed Amr ibn al-Aas as a banner in the Battle of Dhath al-Silsil. (Bukhari 3662, Muslim 1856)"
34298,"(34298) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Amra, she said: The banner of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was white."
34299,"(34299) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Aqeel, he said: Abu Nadhrah narrated to us, he said: He met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. One day he greeted the enemy and said to his companions: Whoever of you comes with a leader, may God grant him whatever he wishes. (Abu Dawud 2961, Bayhaqi 133)"
34300,"(34300) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Adiy bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, who said: The Messenger of God was sent May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to a man who married his father’s wife, so he ordered him to bring him his head."
34301,"(34301) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: Abdullah said: On the day of Badr, I, Saad, and Ammar joined forces, and Saad came with my two heads."
34302,"(34302) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hunaidah ibn Khalid Al-Khuza’i, who said: The first head was sacrificed. In Islam, the head of the foolish son was given to Muawiyah."
34303,"(34303) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Quraya bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib. Al-Misri, he said: He sent Abu Bakr, or Omar, Al-Awza’i doubted, Uqba bin Amir Al-Janni, and Muslimah bin Mukhlid The Ansari went to Egypt, he said: So it was opened for them, he said: So they sent the head of the penguin’s camel, and when he saw it he denied it, so he said: They are doing something like this to us. So he said: Survival of Persia and the Romans? No head is conveyed to us, but the book and the report are sufficient for us of that."
34304,"(34304) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka’b, on the authority of his father, he said: Say The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not travel except on a Thursday. (Bukhari 2949. Abu Dawud 2598)"
34305,"(34305) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Medi ibn Maimun, on the authority of Wasil Mawla Abi Uyaynah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was traveling on Thursday."
34306,"(34306) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Ammarah bin Hadid, on the authority of Sakhr Al-Ghamidi, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Oh God, bless my nation in its first fruits. He said: And whenever he sent a convoy or an army He sent them out at the beginning of the day. He said: Sakhr was a merchant, so he used to send for his trade at the beginning of the day, and his wealth increased.
(Abu Dawud 2599. Tirmidhi 1212)"
34307,"(34307) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: O God, bless my nation in its first birth."
34308,"(34308) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of al-Nu’man bin Sa’d, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: Oh God, bless my nation with its firstborn. (Tirmidhi 478 and Abu Ali 421)"
34309,"(34309) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was Peace and blessings of God be upon him, when he wanted to go on a journey, he would say: Oh God, you are the companion in the journey and the successor in the family. Oh God, you are the companion in the journey and the successor in the family. I seek refuge in You from dullness during travel, and depression during times of upheaval. O God, grant us the land and make travel easy for us."
34310,"(34310) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: A man wanted On a journey, he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, advise me. He said: I advise you to fear God and to magnify God. On all honor."
34311,"(34311) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sargis, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him, when he sets out as a traveler, he seeks refuge from the burdens of travel, the depression of a turning point, and the rain after the rain, and from his supplication. The oppressed, and the one who has a bad outlook regarding his family and wealth."
34312,"(34312) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, he said: Aoun bin Abdullah told me; That a man came to Ibn Masoud and said: I want to travel, so advise me. He said: When you go, say: In the name of God, God is sufficient for me. I put my trust in God, for when you say: In the name of God, the angel says: You have been guided, and when you say: God is sufficient for me, the angel says: You have been preserved. And when you say: I trust in God, the angel says: You are sufficient."
34313,"(34313) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to say in travel: O God, convey the message. Goodness will be attained, forgiveness and satisfaction from you, goodness is in your hand, you are capable of all things, O God, you are the companion in Travel, and the caliph is upon the family. Oh God, expand the earth for us, and make travel easy for us. Oh God, we seek refuge in You from the burdens of travel. And dejected depression, and a bad outlook regarding one’s family and money."
34314,"(34314) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wanted to return, he would say: “I will repent, worship, and praise our Lord.” So when he entered On his family, he said: Repent, repent, our Lord is a helper, He will not leave any repentance against us."
34315,"(34315) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And when he finished a journey, he said the salutation, saying: “Repentant, worshipers, our Lord, praiseworthy.”"
34316,"(34316) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Ubad Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace; He used to say that when he returned from the army, or the company, or Hajj, or the Umrah, whenever he paid it off on a secondment, or he paid it back. He said “Allahu Akbar” three times, then said: There is no god but Allah alone. Allah is true to His promise. We will repent and worship, praise be to our Lord."
34317,"(34317) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, when he departed from the armies, or the companies, or Hajj, or Umrah, then he mentioned something similar."
34318,"(34318) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Anas bin Malik; He was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he was in the outskirts of Medina, or in the heat, the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: We will repent and worship. If God wills, we will be thankful to our Lord."
34319,"(34319) Hushaym told us, he said: The common people told us, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymiy, he said: When they closed their doors, they said: You are repentant, you are thankful to our Lord."
34320,"(34320) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Our people informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Al-Bara’, on the authority of His father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; When he returned from a journey, he would say: “You will repent. To our Lord we will be thankful.”"
34321,"(34321) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade About a man traveling alone."
34322,"(34322) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; Omar forbade the two men to travel."
34323,"(34323) Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He disliked it for a man and two men to travel, except for three and no more."
34324,"(34324) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj ibn Abi Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God was asked May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about a man traveling alone? He said: Satan. It was said: So the two? He said: Two devils. It was said: The three? He said: Companions. (Abu Dawud 2400, Tirmidhi 1674)"
34325,"(34325) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The rider is a devil, and the two riders are two devils. And the three companions."
34326,"(34326) Waki’ told us, he said: A partner told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, that a man should travel alone in the wilderness."
34327,"(34327) Waki’ told us, he said: Asim bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: If people knew what is in being alone, a rider would never travel alone at night."
34328,"(34328) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that a man should travel alone, and that he should spend the night in a house alone."
34329,"(34329) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: Do not spend the night alone, for Satan is the most passionate about you."
34330,"(34330) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Khwat bin Jubayr to the Banu Qurayzah, riding a horse of his own, which is called: Jannah. (Hakim 413)"
34331,"(34331) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, who said: A man said to Mujahid: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: One is a devil, and the two are devils. He said: Mujahid: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has been sent He died alone, and Abdullah and Khabbab sent a convoy, but Omar said: Make three of you on your journeys, and if he dies One has two, one is a devil, and two are devils."
34332,"(34332) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, lest a man go to his family at night, betray them, or seek their faults. (Muslim 1528, Darmi 2631)"
34333,"(34333) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammam bin Yahya, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, On the authority of Anas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not go to his family at night, but he would come to them in the morning, or in the evening
(Bukhari 1800 and Muslim 1527)"
34334,"(34334) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais; He heard Al-Anazi’s barking, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you enter By night, no one will come to his family on his way. Jabir said: By God, we have already made their way to them after that. (Ahmed 2998, Ibn Hibban 2713)"
34335,"(34335) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hamid Al-Araj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim. Al-Taymiyy, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Rawahih, who said: I was on a campaign, so I asked for permission and was in a hurry. So I came to the door, and the lamp was shining, and I saw something white sleeping, so I drew my sword, then She moved it and said: To you, to you. So-and-so was with me and she combed me, so I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I informed him, but he forbade the man from going to his family at night.
(Ahmad 451, Hakim 293)"
34336,"(34336) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab came From his expedition, until he reached the cliff, he said: O people, do not touch women, and do not deceive them. Then he sent a rider to Medina that people are entering for lunch."
34337,"(34337) Abdul Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Amer, who said: Jabir bin Abdullah said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If one of you is absent from his family for a long time, he should not go to his family at night.
(Bukhari 5244, Muslim 182)"
34338,"(34338) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Hafsa bint Sirin, on the authority of Umm Atiyya Al-Ansariyah, she said: I fought with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, seven battles. I succeeded them in their camps, so I will do I give them food, treat the wounded, and take care of the sick. (Muslim 1447. Ahmad 84)"
34339,"(34339) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Rafi’ ibn Salma al-Ashja’i narrated to us, saying: Hashraj ibn Ziyad narrated to me. Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of his grandmother, his father’s mother; She went on a campaign with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the news of six women reached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted us, then he sent for us and said: On whose order did you leave? We saw anger in him, so we said: O Messenger of God, we went out with a medicine to treat him with, and to hand arrows to him, and to give him water to drink. And we spin hair, with which we help in the cause of God. Then he said to us: “Stand up.” When God granted victory to him, he swore to us just as he had sworn For men 
(Abu Dawud 2723. Ahmed 271)"
34340,"(34340) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of al-Zuhri, and Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of Yazid. Ibn Hurmuz said: Najda wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him about women: Were they present with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? May the peace and blessings of God be upon him? Did he hit them with an arrow? Yazid said: I wrote a letter from Ibn Abbas to Najd: They were present with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. As for him hitting them with an arrow, no, and he used to submit to them."
34341,"(34341) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, he said: Sa’id bin Amr narrated to me. Al-Qurashi; Kabsha’s mother was a woman from the Banu Adhirah, Adhirah Quda’i, and she said: O Messenger of God, give me permission to go out. The army of such-and-such. He said: No. She said: O Messenger of God, I do not want to fight. Rather, I want to treat the wounded. And the sick person, and he gave the sick person drink, and he said: Were it not for the fact that it was a Sunnah, and it is said: So-and-so came out, I would have given you permission, but Sit down (Tabarani 431)"
34342,"(34342) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah; Safiyya was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of the ditch."
34343,"(34343) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Al-Awwam ibn Muzahim, on the authority of Khalid ibn Sihan, he said: She witnessed Four or five women were hidden with Abu Musa, including Umm Majza bin Thawr."
34344,"(34344) Khaled bin Harmala Al-Abdi told us, on the authority of Al-Mutharith bint Zaid, the sister of Abu Nadhrah; That Abu Nadrah went on a campaign with his wife Zainab to Khurasan. (Ibn Saad 208)"
34345,"(34345) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Abdullah bin Juma’ told us, he said: My grandmother told me, and Abdul Rahman Ibn Khallad Al-Ansari, on the authority of Umm Warqa bint Nawfal; When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, attacked Badr, she said: I said: O Messenger of God, give me permission to fight with you. I treat your wounded, and nurse your patients, perhaps God will bless me with a witness. He said: Stay in your house, for God He will provide you with the Shahadah. He said: So she was called the Shahidah. (Abu Dawud 592. Daraqutni 111)"
34346,"(34346) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He disliked women going out to any of these private parts, meaning the ports."
34347,"(34347) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Raja’ bin Abi Salamah told me, he said: Mughirah bin Habib told me, he circumcised Malik bin Dinar, he said: I asked Ibn Abdullah, he said: We will enter the land of polytheism, and besiege the fort, and they will fight us fiercely. They asked us for safety, but that prince refused. So what do you think of their fighting? He said: Not to you, that to the prince."
34348,"(34348) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: I heard Amr bin Abi Qais, mentioning on the authority of Mutarrif, he said: I asked Al-Hakam, I said: The king from the kings of Khorasan reconciles with those of captivity over known heads? He said: As long as there is peace, there is no problem."
34349,"(34349) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Dhi Haddan, on the authority of those who heard Ali, He says: God called the war on the tongue of His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a deception. (Bukhari 3029, Muslim 1362)"
34350,"(34350) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id bin Dhu Haddan, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, he said: God has judged on the tongue of His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. War is a deception, and I am a warrior who speaks about war. He said: But if I say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, By God, there is nothing else more beloved to me than the heavens than to say something about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, what he did not say. (Ahmad 90. Ibn Saad 244)"
34351,"(34351) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka’b ibn Malik, on the authority of his father He said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to launch a campaign, he would see something else. (Bukhari 2947, Abu Dawud 2630)"
34352,"(34352) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, he heard Jabir say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, God He brings people out of the fire after they had become lava. He said: And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: War is a deception.
(Bukhari 3030, Muslim 1361)"
34353,"(34353) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Khaythamiya, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafali, he said: Ali said: If I told you about what was between me and you, for war is a deception, and if I told you about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Because something lower than the heavens is more beloved to me than to lie. (Bukhari 3611, Muslim 154)"
34354,"(34354) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: War is a deception. (Ibn Majah 2833)"
34355,"(34355) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Qais, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent Amr ibn al-Aas greeted Dhat al-Silsil during his campaign, but they were struck by severe cold. He said: No man should light a fire, and then fight the people. When they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, they complained about this to him, and he said: O Messenger of God, there were few among my companions. And I feared that the people would see your smallness, and their intention to follow the enemy for fear that they would be ambushed by Behind the mountain, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was amazed at that. (Hakim 43)"
34356,"(34356) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Mundhir bin Tha’labă narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, he said: Omar told my father Bakr, when Amr did not let the people light a fire, do you not see this one who prevented the people from benefiting from them? He said: Then Abu said Bakr: He left him, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed him as governor over us because of his knowledge of war."
34357,"(34357) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, plotted on the day One of the polytheists, and it was the first day on which he deceived them."
34358,"(34358) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayd, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abjar, who said: A man, who is called: Subaih: We were in Al-Fateh with Ali. He said: Ali was a tried man. He used to say: War is a deception. He said: Then he came to the rock. He said: Then he said: God is Great. God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. He rocked him. He said: So we will see that it is Something was said to him. He said: Then he came to the quagmire, and he said: He was quack, God is great. God and His Messenger have spoken the truth, so we will see. We are saying that it is something that was said to him."
34359,"(34359) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, he said: The war deceived him."
34360,"(34360) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr. On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: My father, who breastfed me from the children of Mara, told me: It is as if I were looking at Jafar. On the day of his death, he mounted a horse that had a blond hair and necked it, then he went on and fought until he was killed."
34361,"(34361) Yahya bin Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais, or Others, he said: He sent Abu Bakr to the Levant and said: Do not hamper any animal, you will be distressed by its waters."
34362,"(34362) Waki’ told us, he said: Ma’qil bin Ubaid Allah Al-Absi told us, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, he said: Al-Hasir, no. He is sterilized."
34363,"(34363) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Hudhali narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: When the guards were sent, it was said to them: Do not deprive the poor."
34364,"(34364) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Qays, on the authority of Mughirah ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Ubaad ibn He forgot, he said: Abu Bakr said: Do not hamper an animal, even if you are distressed."
34365,"(34365) Waki` bin al-Jarrah narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Hamid bin Abd. Al-Rahman Al-Himyari, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever finds an animal on your property, it belongs to whom? He revived her."
34366,"(34366) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man leaving his beast in the wasteland, he said: It is for the one who saved it."
34367,"(34367) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man who left his animal, and a man took it. He said: Then its owner came and disputed with him to Amir, and he said: This matter has been decided. Before today, if he slew it in fear and for a reward, then he has more right to his animal, even if he slew it in pasture. And he is secure, but he has no right to it."
34368,"(34368) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, he said: Shuabi told us, on the authority of Abi Al-Fayd, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr Al-Ra'ini, on the authority of his father, I think; Abu Bakr sent an army, so he walked with them and said: Praise be to God, whose feet are covered with dust in the path of God. He said, so he said A man: We only sent them on their way, and he said: We prepared them, sent them on their way, and called for them."
34369,"(34369) Ibn Abi Ghani told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, or someone else, who said: He was sent Abu Bakr sent an army to the Levant and went out to accompany them on his camel."
34370,"(34370) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. It was said to him: Ja`far has come, and he said: I do not know which of them I will be happy with. With the arrival of Jafar, or with the conquest of Khaybar? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, met him and embraced him, and accepted what was between his eyes."
34371,"(34371) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Hanash bin Al-Harith narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: When Omar directed us to Al-Kufa, he walked with us for an hour during the day, bid us farewell and prayed for us, then sat down and dusted off his feet, then returned."
34372,"(34372) Abu Bakr narrated to us, he said, I narrated, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked with Ali but did not meet him."
34373,"(34373) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Quraysh, who said: We took Omar to Sarrar."
34374,"(34374) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla. He said: Abdullah bin Omar told me; He was in one of the companies of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the people looked for his rations, and I was among those who gathered. He said Then we said when we fled: What shall we do when we have fled from the advance, and we have been filled with wrath? So we said: We will enter Medina and spend the night there, but no one will see us. He said: When we entered, we said: If we had presented ourselves to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then if we had repentance, we would have remained steadfast. If other than that, we would go. He said: We sat with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, before the lunch prayer. When Our people went out to him, and we said: O Messenger of God, we are fleeing. He said: Then he approached us and said: Rather, you are the Akkarun. He said: So we approached, kissed his hand, and said: O Messenger of God, we wanted to do it, and for us to do it. He said: I am the group of Muslims.
(Abu Dawud 2440, Tirmidhi 1716)"
34375,"(34375) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: When the age of killing of Abu Ubaidah reached Al-Thaqafi, he said: If I were his side, even if he sided with me."
34376,"(34376) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Omar said: I am the class of all Muslim"
34377,"(34377) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It has reached Omar that a people were patient. In Azerbaijan until they were killed, then Omar said: If they had sided with me, I would have been their faction."
34378,"(34378) Waki’ told us, he said: Hassan bin Salih told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever flees from three has not fled, and whoever flees from two has fled, meaning from crawling."
34379,"(34379) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Mughirah Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Malik bin Jarir, On the authority of Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, he said: Fleeing from the march is a major sin."
34380,"(34380) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ikrimah bin Ammar narrated to us, on the authority of Taysla bin Ali Al-Badali, on the authority of Ibn Omar, He said: Fleeing from the march is a major sin."
34381,"(34381) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari; He saw a man who had turned his back, and he said to him: The heat of fire is more severe than the heat of the sword."
34382,"(34382) Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Al-Taymimi told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: When Abu Ubaid was killed and defeated His companions, he said: Omar said: I am your group."
34383,"(34383) Dhu narrated to us, saying: Awf narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; {And whoever is in charge of them on that day will turn away}. He said: It was revealed about the people of Badr."
34384,"(34384) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin told us Abi Laila; Two men fled on the day of a dwelling from the city of Kufa, so they came to ‘Amr, and he insulted them and took them by force with his tongue. Severe, and he said: Did you escape? And he wanted to divert them to the point of Basra, so they said: O Commander of the Faithful, no, but rather return us to the point that We fled from him, so that our repentance might come from him."
34385,"(34385) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin and I were repeated. Al-Harith about the Day of the Camel, belittle us."
34386,"(34386) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He showed me The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was in the fight on the day of Uhud when I was fourteen years old. He looked down on me, so he turned me away. Then He presented me with the day of the ditch when I was fifteen years old, and he rewarded me. Nafi’ said: I narrated that to Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz, and he Caliph, and he said: This is a demarcation between the young and the great, so he wrote to his workers: Whoever has reached the age of fifteen, then impose For him in the fighting, and whoever is less than that, make provisions for him in the household. (Bukhari 2444, Muslim 1490)"
34387,"(34387) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik Ibn Umair, he said: I heard Atiyya al-Qurazi He says: We presented it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Qurayz, and whoever produced it was killed, and whoever did not produce it. He was not killed, so I was among those who did not return, so they did not kill me."
34388,"(34388) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: I and Ibn Umar were presented to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Badr, so we looked down, and we witnessed someone. (Bukhari 3955. Tahawi 219)"
34389,"(34389) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abd Al-Aziz bin Abi Al-Sa’ba, on the authority of Abu Aflah Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zurur Al-Ghafiqi, on the authority of Ali, who said: A white mule was given to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: O Messenger of God, if we wished we could take from We did this. He said: How? We said: We load the donkeys on the well-bred horses and you bring them. He said: Only those who do not know do that.
(Bayhaqi 23)"
34390,"(34390) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Omar bin Husail, on the authority of Amer, who said: It was given to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, a white mule. Then Dihiya al-Kalbi said: If we wished, O Messenger of God, we could take something like it. He said: And how? He said: We load the donkeys on the well-bred horses and you bring them. He said: Only those who do not know do that.
(Tabarani 4993. Ahmad 311)"
34391,"(34391) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, he said: He wrote Omar bin Abdul Aziz came to us, and his letter was read to us: “Whoever carries a donkey on a horse’s carriage, wipe out His gift is ten dinars."
34392,"(34392) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Jadham, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a donkey from riding on a horse. (Tirmidhi 1701, Ahmed 225)"
34393,"(34393) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Salim bin Abi al-Ja`d, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the use of a donkey on a horse. (Ahmed 95)"
34394,"(34394) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Omar bin Husayl narrated to us, saying: I heard Al-Sha’abi saying: Dahiya Al-Kalbi said: O Messenger of God, shall we not set a donkey on a horse, and it will produce a foal that we can ride? He said: Only those who do not know do that."
34395,"(34395) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’d bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Salami, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a convoy, and appointed a man from the Ansar over them, so he ordered them to They listen to him and obey him. He said: They made him angry about something. He said: Gather firewood for me. So they gathered firewood for him. He said: Burn a fire. A fire, so they kindled a fire. He said: Didn’t he command you to listen to me and obey me? They said: Yes, he said: So enter it. He said: Then they looked at each other and said: We only fled to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he was saved from the fire.
 He said: While they were like that, his anger subsided and the fire was extinguished. He said: When they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace They mentioned that to him, and he said: If they had entered it, they would not have left it. Rather, obedience is in what is right. (Bukhari 4340 and Muslim 1470)"
34396,"(34396) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, that Abdullah narrated to him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: It is the duty of a Muslim to listen and obey, in what he likes and dislikes, as long as he is not commanded to disobey Him, so whoever commands Because of his disobedience, he will neither be heard nor obeyed. (Bukhari 2955, Muslim 1469)"
34397,"(34397) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Hakam bin Thawban, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Alqamah ibn Mujaz to go on a mission while I was with them. When he arrived at the head of the battles, Or it was in some way that a group of the army asked for permission, so he gave them permission and appointed Abdullah bin Hudhafiya bin Qais Al-Sahmi, and I was among those who invaded with him. Then, while on the way, the people kindled a fire to warm themselves up, or to do something nice with it, and Abdullah said, “And it was There is a joke in it: Is it not my duty to listen and obey you? They said: Yes, he said: I do not command you to do anything unless you do it? They said: Yes. He said: I am determined that you will not jump into this Fire. Then some people got up and took shelter. When he thought that they had And jump. He said: Hold yourselves, for I am only joking with you. When we came, they mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Whoever of them commands you to disobey him, do not obey him. (Ibn Majah 2863, Hakim 630)"
34398,"(34398) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Salami, on the authority of Ali, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no obedience to a human being in disobedience to God. (Bukhari 7257, Muslim 1469)"
34399,"(34399) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: No obedience. To preach disobedience to God."
34400,"(34400) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafli, he said: Omar said to me: O Abu Umayyah, I do not know whether I will not meet you after this year of mine, so listen and obey, even if a servant is appointed over you. A dreadful Abyssinian. If he strikes you, be patient. If he deprives you, be patient. If he wants something that will diminish your religion, then say: Listen and obey, my blood. Without my religion, do not separate from the community."
34401,"(34401) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Mis`ar narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Abu Sadiq al-Azdi, on the authority of Rabi` bin Najid, on the authority of Ali, said: Indeed, the Quraysh are the imams of the Arabs, their righteous ones are their righteous imams, and their immoral ones are their imams. They are unjust, and each has a right, so give each person his due, unless one of you has a choice between becoming a Muslim and beheading him. So if one of you has the choice between his conversion to Islam and beheading, let him stretch out his neck, for his mother is bereaved of him, for he has neither this world nor any The last after his conversion to Islam."
34402,"(34402) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Amara, he said: Atris bin Arqoub, or Ma’add, said: Al-A’mash doubted. He said: I do not care whether I obeyed a man in disobeying God, or whether I prostrated to this tree."
34403,"(34403) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ammar, he said: Ma’add descended next to a tree, and he said: What I care if I obeyed a man in disobedience to God, or prostrated to this tree instead of God."
34404,"(34404) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: His people informed us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Maraya, on the authority of Imran ibn Husayn said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: There is no obedience in disobedience to God. (Ahmad 66. Tayalisi 856)"
34405,"(34405) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Salam bin Miskin narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Whenever Omar employed a man He wrote in his covenant: Listen to him and obey what he has done to you. He said, when he used Hudhayf, it was written in his covenant: Listen. And obey Him, and give Him what He asked of you. He said: So Hudhayf Al-Mada'in came on a donkey, with a loaf of bread and his sweat in his hand.
 Waki` said: Malik said, on the authority of Talha: He pulled his feet to one side.
 Salam said: When he read his covenant to them, they said: Ask us. He said: I ask you for food that I may eat, and fodder for this donkey of mine. He said: So he stayed among them as long as God wished, then Omar wrote to him to come, so he left, and when Omar reached his arrival, he remained in wait for him in a place where He saw him, and when he saw him in the state in which he left him, Omar came to him, and he joined him and said: You are his brother and I am your brother."
34406,"(34406) Waki’ told us, he said: Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: No obedience. For a created being in disobedience to the Creator."
34407,"(34407) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amara, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad; Habib bin Zayd was killed by his Muslim brother, and when it was the day of Al-Yamamah, his brother Abdullah bin Zayd and his mother came out. His mother had vowed not to wash her hair until his Muslim man was killed, so they went out among the people. Abdullah bin Zaid said: I made it my business, so I attacked him and stabbed him with a spear. He walked towards me with the spear and said: And a man from among the people called to me: He rewarded him with the spear. He said: He did not understand. He said, so he called him: To throw the spear from your hand. He said: So he threw the spear from his hand and was defeated. Muslim"
34408,"(34408) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Thumamah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Anas, who said: I came to Thabit ibn Qais on the day of the dove, while he was being mummified, so I said: Uncle, don’t you see what the people encountered? He said: Now, my nephew."
34409,"(34409) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Walid Al-Muzani, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Utba, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I came to Abdullah bin Makhramah, struck down on the day of Al-Yamama, so I stood over him, and he said: O Abdullah bin Omar, does a fasting person break his fast? I said: Yes. He said: So make water for me in this chamber, so that I may break my fast. He said: So I came to the basin and it was filled with blood. So I hit him with my fist, then I took a nap from him and came to him, and found that he had finished."
34410,"(34410) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thumama bin Anas, on the authority of Anas, he said: I was in the hands of Khalid bin Al-Walid and Al-Baraa on the day of Al-Yamamah. He said: Then Khaled sent horses, and they came. Defeated, he said: And he made Al-Baraa’ thunder, so I made him throw him to the ground while he was saying, “I find myself breaking my fast.” He said: Then he was sent Khaled the horses and they came defeated. He said: Then Khaled looked at the heavens, then he went down to the earth, and he would do that if he wanted. The matter, then he said: O Innocence, he is alone in himself. He said: So he said: Now? He said: So he said: Yes, now. He said: So Al-Baraa mounted his horse and started hitting it with the whip, as if I was looking at it and... She was licking her sins, so he thanked God and praised him, and said: O people of Medina, there is no Medina for you, but He is God alone and Paradise. Then he carried and carried the people with him, and the people of Al-Yamam were defeated, until he reached their fortress. Then Muhakim Al-Yamamah met him and said: O Innocence. So he struck him with the sword, and Al-Bara’ avoided him with the sword, so he struck the sword. Then Al-Baraa struck him and knocked him down, so he took the sword of Mohkam Al-Yamamah and struck him with it until it broke, and he said: May God curse what is left of you. He threw it away and returned to his sword."
34411,"(34411) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Al-Zubayr used to follow the killers. On the Day of Al-Yamamah, when he saw a man lying with his eyes, he passed by him, saying: Then he came to a man lying with the dead. So he went to him with the sword, and when he felt it, he touched the sword and jumped up and ran, and Al-Zubayr ran after him, saying: I am the son of Safiyya Al-Muhajir said: Then the man turned to him and said: How do you see the hardship of your infidel brother? He said: So he besieged him until he escaped."
34412,"(34412) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ubaid bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad bin Al-Hadd said: Salem, the client of Abu Hudhayfah, was injured on the Day of Al-Yamamah."
34413,"(34413) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: It was the slogan of the Muslims on the day of their conversion, oh Companions of Surah Al-Baqarah."
34414,"(34414) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: There was an apostasy among Banu Sulaym, so he sent Abu Bakr Khalid bin Al-Walid came to them, and he gathered some of them into a barn and burned them with fire, and that age reached the age of So he came to Abu Bakr and said: Remove a man who is being tortured with the punishment of God. Abu Bakr said: By God, I will not bear a sword. May God bless him. His enemy, until God is his name, and he commanded him, so he proceeded from that to his peace."
34415,"(34415) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thumam bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Anas; That Khalid bin Al-Walid directed the people on the Day of Al-Yamamah, so they came to Nahar and put the bottoms of their cellars in detention. Then they cut off to them, and they gathered together, and the Muslims turned back, and Khaled bowed down quickly, then he raised his head, and I was with him. And among the innocences, and when Khalid was accompanied by a matter, he would look at the heavens for a moment, then raise his head to the heavens, and then he would be rewarded. He saw it, so Al-Baraa’ started to lose his mind, so I made him push him to the ground, and he said: O son of my brother, I am breaking my fast. Then he said: O Al-Baraa’. Get up. Al-Baraa’ said: Now? He said: Yes, now. Al-Baraa’ mounted a female horse, and he thanked God and praised Him, then said: As for what follows, O people, what There is a way to Medina, but that is Paradise, so he entered them for an hour, then gave his horse a hard time, as if he saw it being sucked. Because of her sin, then he suffered and the people suffered.
 Hammad bin Salamah said: Then Ubaid Allah bin Abi Bakr informed me, on the authority of Anas, he said: There was a furrow in their city, so he put The ruler of the dove, with his feet on it, and he was so great and mighty that he began to shake. I am the ruler of the dove, I am the orbit of the glory. And I and I.
 He said: He was a violent man, so when he was able to strike him, he struck him, and Al-Bara’ protected him with his shin, then Al-Bara’ struck him in the leg. So he killed him, and Muhakim al-Yamamah had a wide plate with him, so he dropped his sword and took Muhakim’s plate, carried it and struck it with it. Until it broke, and he said: May God disgrace what is between you and me, and he took his sword."
34416,"(34416) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Mis`ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awn al-Thaqafi, on the authority of a man he did not name; When Abu Bakr came to him, he opened the dove and prostrated."
34417,"(34417) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mujalid told us, he said: Amir told us, he said: Khalid wrote to the satraps of Persia And he was in bewilderment and he brought it to Bani Buqayla. Amer said: And I read it to Bani Buqayla:
In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful
 From Khaled bin Al-Walid to the satraps of Persia, peace be upon whoever follows guidance, for indeed I praise you, Allah, the One who has no god but Him. Except him, as for after praising God who dispersed your service, dispersed your speech, weakened your rule, and took away your kingdom, then This letter of mine has come to you, so send to me with the pledge, and be free from my obligation, and return to me the tribute, but if not Do so, for by God, there is no god but Him, I will bring to you a people who love death as you love life, and peace. On the one who follows the guidance.
(Abu Ubaid 86)"
34418,"(34418) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Zaydah, on the authority of Khaled bin Salma al-Qurashi, on the authority of Amer Al-Shabi said: Khalid bin Al-Walid wrote to the satraps of Persia at the time of Hira:
In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful
 From Khalid bin Al-Walid to the satraps of Persia, peace be upon whoever follows guidance. As for what follows: Indeed, I praise God, who has not There is no god but Him. Praise be to God who dispersed your service, separated you, and differed between your words. So when he comes to you This is my letter, so beware of my obligation, and respond to the penalty, but if you do not do it, I will come to you with a people who love me. Death is your love for life."
34419,"(34419) Ja`far bin Aoun told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Abu al-Sifar, he said: When Khalid bin al-Walid came to Al-Hira, it was revealed to the Banu al-Marzab, saying: The poison was brought to him, so he took it and put it in his comfort, and said: In the name of God, So he attacked him, but did not harm him at all, God willing. (Abu Ali 7150)"
34420,"(34420) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Hassan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, on the authority of his father, He said: We made an agreement with the people of Al-Hira over a thousand dirhams and a saddlebag. He said: I said: O my father, what did you do with the saddlebags? He said: Our companion did not have a mount."
34421,"(34421) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: When Khalid ibn al-Walid came here, behold, he was armed with the people of Fares, there came upon them a man called: Hazar Mard. He said: They mentioned the greatness of his character and his courage. He said: Khalid bin al-Walid killed him. Then he called for his lunch, and he ate his lunch while leaning on his body, meaning his body."
34422,"(34422) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wa’il; That Khaled bin Al-Walid wrote:
In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful
 From Khalid bin Al-Walid to Rustum, Miran, and the people of Persia, peace be upon whoever follows guidance. Indeed, I praise God, who does not There is no god but Him. As for what follows: I present to you Islam, and if you acknowledge it, then you have what the people of Islam have, and upon you is what the people of Islam have. On the people of Islam, and if you refuse, then I offer to you the tribute. If you acknowledge the tribute, then you will have what For the people of the jizyah, and you are responsible for the people of the jizyah, and if you refuse, then I have men who love to fight as you love Knight of wine"
34423,"(34423) Abu Usama told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qais, he said: I heard Khalid bin Al-Walid talk In confusion, on the day of death."
34424,"(34424) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, who said: I heard Abu Amr Al-Shaybani say: It was Māran was at the beginning of the year, and Al-Qadisiyah was at the end of the year, so Rustom came and said: Mārān was just doing something special. Boys"
34425,"(34425) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: Abu Ubaid bin Masoud crossed the Euphrates to Mihran, so they cut the bridge behind him, and killed him and his companions. He said: So he entrusted him to Omar ibn al-Khattab. He said: So he eulogized him. Abu Mihjan Al-Thaqafi, and he said:
Abu Jabr spent the evening alone in his homes
Abu Amr passed by the bridge from them.
And you continued until you were the last smelling
And even ?

Because the hungry covered widows
In addition to the verses, Hazm and Nael
And the righteous people around me were killed
The elephant has thorns in its throat."
34426,"(34426) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, who said: Abu Ubaid bin Masoud passed by on the day of Maran in People, so the bridge was cut off from them, and they were injured. He said: Qays said: When it was the day of Muharran, people among them said: Khaled bin Arfatah To Jarir: O Jarir, no, by God, we do not see this group of ours. So he said: O Jarir, let us go to them. So I said: Do you want to do to us what they did to Abu Ubaid? We are a people who are not willing to move forward, or to throw themselves off the cross until God judges between us and them. So He passed it. The polytheists, and on that day, Mahran was struck while he was by the palm trees."
34427,"(34427) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: Jarir said to me: Go with us to Miran. So I went with him to where they fought, and he said to me: You saw me here like the burning of fire, and they were stabbing me from the ground. Every side was hit by your meteors. When I saw your destruction, I started saying: O my horse, no, O Jarir. So they heard my voice and I came. Qays, nothing will stop them until you free me. I said: I have passed a month, and no side is higher to me than the impact of a meteor. He said: Qais said: You saw us entering the Degree, and the gates of cities were closed."
34428,"(34428) Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Al-Taymimi told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: When Abu Ubaid was killed and defeated His companions, Omar said: I am your group."
34429,"(34429) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: When the age of Umar came, Abu Ubaid al-Thaqafi was killed. He said: If I were his class, even if he sided with me."
34430,"(34430) Mahboub Al-Qawariri narrated to us, on the authority of Hanash bin Al-Harith Al-Nakha’i, who said: The sheikhs of Al-Nakha’ narrated to us; When Jarir killed Mihran, he set up, or raised his head on a spear."
34431,"(34431) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim; He passed by a man on the day of Abu Ubaid, and his hands and feet had been cut off, and he was saying: {With those to whom God has bestowed blessings. Of the prophets, and the truthful, and the martyrs, and the righteous, and those are good companions.} Then some of those who passed by him said to him: Who are you? He said: A man from the Ansar."
34432,"(34432) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: I witnessed Al-Qadisiyah, and Saad was in charge of the people. Then Rustum came and made Amr bin Maadi Karb al-Zubaidi pass by the rows and say: O Muhajireen, be black. Mighty, for the lion is the one who is most prosperous, and the Persian is the he-goat after it has been struck by a meteorite. He said: And he was with them. Walls against which no arrows can fall. So we said to him: O Abu Thawr, fear that man. He said: We will say that man when he shot us and hit. He mounted his horse, so Amr carried him and embraced him, then he slaughtered him, so he took his clothes, the gold bracelets that were on him, and his belt. And brocade curtains.
 A man fled from Thaqif, and he was alone with the polytheists, so he told them, and said: The people are on this side, and he pointed to Bajil, he said: They threw sixteen elephants at us, with the fighters on them, and two elephants at the rest of the people. He said: It was Saad. On that day, He will say: They shunned it for its generosity. Qays said: We were a quarter of the people on the day of al-Qadisiyah, so Omar gave us a quarter of the black, so we took him for three years.
 After that, Jarir came to Omar, and Ammar bin Yasser was with him. Omar said: Will you not tell me about these two houses of yours? However, I am asking you both, and I will see in your faces which of the two revelations is better? He said: Then Jarir said: I am telling you, O Commander of the Faithful, as for one of the two houses, it is the nearest black palm tree to the land of The Arabs, and as for the other abode, it is the land of Persia, Akkaha, Harraha, and Baqaha, meaning Medina. He said: Ammar denied me, so he said He said: You lied. Omar said: You lied. He said: Then he said: Will you not tell me about this prince of yours? Is he acceptable? They said: No, by God, he is not daring, nor sufficient, nor knowledgeable in politics. So he dismissed him and sent Al-Mughiriya bin Shu’bah."
34433,"(34433) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: Saad had complained of an ulcer on his leg. At that time, he did not go out to fight. He said: She was one of the people who was exposed. He said: Sa’d’s wife said: She was Before him, under Al-Muthanna bin Haritha Al-Shaybani: There are no twenties for horses, so Saad slapped them, and they said: Cowardice and jealousy. He said: Then We defeated them."
34434,"(34434) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays; That Saad’s wife was called: Salma bint Khusfa, and the wife of a man from Banu Shayban was called: Al-Muthanna. Ibn Al-Haritha, and she mentioned something about the matter of Muthanna, so Saad slapped her, and she said: Cowardice and jealousy."
34435,"(34435) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: Saad was brought to Abu Mihjan on the day of Qadisiyah, and he had drunk alcohol, so he was ordered to be chained. He said: Saad was wounded. He did not go out to the people that day. He said: They took him up on top of the grave so that he could look at the people. He said: And he rode the horses. Khaled bin Arfatah, when the people met, Abu Mihjan said:
It is sad enough to kill horses with cannas"
34436,"(34436) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awani narrated to us, he said: Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: Saad bin Abi came. Storyteller until Al-Qadisiyyah came down with the people, and he said: I do not know whether we will not exceed seven thousand, or eight thousand. In between, the polytheists were sixty thousand, or so, with elephants. He said: When they came down, they said to us: Go back. We do not see that you have numbers, nor do we see that you have any strength or weapons, so return. He said: We said: We will not return. He said: And they made They laugh at our nobility and say, “Dooq.” They liken us to spinners. He said, “When we refused to do so, they said, ‘Send. We have brought to us a sane man who will inform us of the one who brought you from your country, for we do not see that you have a number or an enemy.
 He said: Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba said: I am. He said: So he crossed over to them. He said: So he sat with Rustom on the bed. He said: So they bowed down and they bowed down. When he sat with him on the bed, he said: Al-Mughirah said: By God, this gathering of mine has not increased me, nor has your companion diminished. He said: He said: Tell me what brought you from your country, for I do not see a number of you, or a number of others? He said: So he said: We were a people in misery and misguidance, so God sent among us our Prophet, and God guided us upon his path, and provided for us. His hands,And while He provided us with grain, they claimed that it grows on this land, but when we ate from it and fed from it our families They said: There is no good for us until you leave this country and we eat this grain.
 He said: Then Rustum said: Then we will kill you. He said: Then he said: If you kill us, we will enter Paradise, and if we kill you, you will enter Hell. Otherwise You have given the jizyah. He said: When he said: You have given the jizyah, he said: They woke up and snorted and said: There is no peace between us and you. Al-Mughirah said: Will you cross over to us, or shall we cross over to you? He said: So Rustum said: Rather, we will cross to you. He said: So the Muslims delayed until some of them crossed over. He said: So he carried The Muslims were upon them, so they killed them and defeated them.
 Husayn said: Their king was Rustam from the people of Azerbaijan.
 Husayn said: I heard an old man from us, called Ubaid bin Jahsh, saying: You saw us walking on the backs of men. We cross the trench on the backs of men, as long as no weapon touches us.
 Some of them had killed others. He said: We found a coffin containing camphor. He said: We thought it was salt. We had no doubt that it was salt. He said: So we cooked meat and put some of it into it, but when we found no taste for it, then one of my servants passed by us with a shirt. He said: So he said: O community of those who cross over,Do not spoil your food, for there is no good in the salt of this earth. May I give you this shirt, He said: So he gave us a shirt with it, so we gave it to a friend of ours and he wore it. He said: So we made us admire it and admire it. He said: So, the price The shirt, when we knew the clothes, was two dirhams. He said: And you saw me pointing to a man, and that he was wearing two bracelets of gold, and that his weapons were under a grave of those. The graves, and I pointed to him, and he came out to us and said: He did not speak to us, nor did we speak to him, until we beheaded him, and we defeated them. Until they reached the Euphrates. He said: So we rode and sought them, but they were defeated. Until they reached Syria. He said: So we sought them, but they were defeated. Until they came to Al-Saraha. He said: So We sought them, and they were defeated until they came to Al-Mada'in. He said: So we camped as a camp. He said: And armed for the polytheists with a load of weapons, the horses of the Muslims would come to them and fight them, but their armed men were defeated. The polytheists, until they joined the cities.
 The Muslims walked until they landed on the shore of the Tigris, and a group of Muslims crossed from Kalawadhi, or from below, from Medina. So they besieged them until they could find no food except their dogs and their hooks. He said: So they endured during the night until they came to Julaila. He said: Saad went to them with the people.Based on the introduction of Hashim bin Utbah, he said: And this is the event that occurred. He said: So God destroyed them, and he set off. Then let them go to Nayavand. He said: Abu Wael said: When the polytheists were defeated from Jalawla, they came to Nawand. He said: So Omar bin Al-Khattab appointed Ali. The people of Kufa are Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, and the people of Basra are Mujashi bin Masoud Al-Salami. He said: Amr bin Maadi came to him. He was distressed, so he said to him: Give me a horse like me, and a weapon like me. He said: Yes, I will give you from my money. He said: So Amr bin said to him: Contagious anguish: By God, we have come to you, but we have not given you understanding, and we have fought you, but we have not answered you, and we have asked of you, and we have not answered you. We have made you miserly. Husayn said: Al-Numan bin Muqrin was Ali Kaskar. He said: So he wrote to Omar: O Commander of the Faithful, indeed my example and his Kaskar is like a young man in the presence of a prostitute. She is colored and perfumed, and I adjure you by God when you have separated me from Kaskar. And you sent me in an army of the Muslim armies. He said: So he wrote to him: Go to the people in Banhavand, and you will be upon them.
 He said: So he walked towards them. He said: They met, and he was the first to be killed. He said: Suwayd bin Muqrin took the banner, so God granted them victory. And God destroyed the polytheists, and no group was established for them after that time.He said: And the people of all Egypt were marching toward their enemy and their country.
 Husayn said: When the polytheists were defeated from Al-Madain, he pursued them with Jalula, then he returned and sent Ammar bin Yasir, so he marched until He camped in Al-Mada'in, he said: And he wanted to visit it with the people, but the people came to it and disliked it, so it reached Umar that the people disliked it. He asked: Are camels suitable for this? They said: No, because there are mosquitoes in it. He said: Then Omar said: The Arabs are not suitable for a land where camels are not suitable. He said: So they returned. He said: He met Saad Ibadia, he said: So he said: I direct you to a land that rose from the grass, protruded from the marsh, and was located in the middle of the countryside. And it was stabbed in the nose of Al-Biriya. He said: A land between Al-Hira and the Euphrates."
34437,"(34437) Ibn Abi Za’idah told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Omar wrote to Sa’ad on the day of Al-Qadisiyah: Indeed, I have sent to you the people of the Hijaz and the people of Yemen, so whoever of them catches up with the fighting before they disperse, then contribute. Oh God!"
34438,"(34438) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Abi Hind, who said: A man said on the Day of Al-Qadisiyah: Oh God, is my Hadith a black one? So he married me today to a beautiful virgin. Then he came forward and was killed. He said: They passed by him while he was embracing a great man."
34439,"(34439) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’d bin Ibrahim, he said: They passed by a man on the Day of Al-Qadisiyah. His hands and feet were cut off, and he was being examined, and he said: “With those to whom God has bestowed favors among the prophets and the truthful.” And the martyrs and the righteous, and those are good companions.} He said: Then he said: What are you, O Abdullah? He said: I am a man from the Ansar."
34440,"(34440) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: Omar ordered me to call him. In Al-Qadisiyyah: It is not rejected in the case of daba’a, nor hantam, nor zifat."
34441,"(34441) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: A letter from Abu Bakr came to us in Al-Qadisiyah, and he wrote Abdullah bin Al-Arqam."
34442,"(34442) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais Al-Abdi, on the authority of Shubr bin Alqamiya, he said: When it was the Day of Qadisiyah, a man from the people of Persia rose up and called for a duel. He mentioned his greatness, so a man stood up to him. Short. It was said to him: Shabar bin Alqamiya. He said: Then the Persian said to him like this, meaning he carried him, then struck him. He hit the ground and knocked him down. He said: Then a span of time took a dagger that the Persian had with him, and said thus and so with it in his stomach, meaning So he subdued him, saying: Then he turned against him and killed him, then he brought his plunder to Saad, so he gathered twelve thousand, and Saad sent him off. Oh, oh"
34443,"(34443) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Qays, on the authority of Shubr ibn Alqamiya, who said: I fought a man one day. Al-Qadisiyah was one of the non-Arabs. I killed him, took his loot, and brought him to Sa’d. Sa’d addressed his companions, then said: This is his loot. A span, which is better than twelve thousand dirhams, and indeed We have granted it to him."
34444,"(34444) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of the one who witnessed Al-Qadisiyyah, he said: Among us was a man who took a bath when he examined his So he went to Saad and told him, and he said: Put it among the spoils of the Muslims."
34445,"(34445) Abbad told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of those who realized that; That a man bought a slave girl from the spoils, and he said: When she saw that she was devoted to him, she took out a lot of jewelry that she had with her. He said: Then the man said: I do not know what this is, until he went to Saad and asked him, and he said: Put it among the spoils of the Muslims."
34446,"(34446) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Makhramah, he said: Saad sold a basin for a thousand dirhams to a man from the people of Al-Hira, and he was told: Omar heard this from you and found it wrong. He said: He continued to ask the Christian, until he returned the basin to him and took the thousand."
34447,"(34447) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Al-Sabah bin Thabit narrated to us, saying: The sheikhs of the neighborhood narrated to us, Jarir bin Abdullah: It has come upon the Qadisiyah River for three hours of daylight, and it only flows with blood, from what we have killed. The polytheists"
34448,"(34448) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Hanash bin Al-Harith narrated to us, saying: I heard my father mentioning, he said: When we came from Yemen: We camped in Medina, and Omar came out against us. He went around the Nakha’ and looked at them and said: O people of the Nakha’, I see. The cypress is among you spread out, and over you is Iraq and the masses of Persia. So we said: O Commander of the Faithful, no, but rather to the Levant, we want to migrate. To it, he said: No, but rather Iraq, for I have satisfied it for you. He said: Some of us even said: O Commander of the Faithful, no. Compulsion in religion. He said: There is no compulsion in religion. You should go to Iraq. He said: There is hunger among the non-Arabs, and we are two thousand. And five hundred. He said: Then we came to Al-Qadisiyah, and one of the Nakha's was killed, and such and such and such and such, and eighty of the rest of the people, so Omar said: : What about the Nakha’, were they injured among the rest of the people? Did people flee from them? They said: No, rather they left the greatness of the matter alone."
34449,"(34449) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hanash ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of his father, who said: The palm tree passed by Omar, so he came to them. So he looked at them, and they were two thousand and five hundred, and there was a man over them, called Artaha, and he said: I see the joy in you. Cross-legged, walk to your brothers from Iraq, and they said: No, rather we will march to the Levant. He said: Walk to Iraq, and they said: No. He was forced into religion, so he said: Go to Iraq. When they came to Iraq, they withheld the dowry and slaughtered it. So he wrote To them: make amends, for in the matter there is a stronghold, or a soul."
34450,"(34450) And I heard Abu Bakr ibn Ayash saying: Banu Asad was four hundred on the day of al-Qadisiyah, and there were By his generation, there were three thousand, and Nakha was two thousand and three hundred, and Canada was near Nakha, and they were all Ten thousand, and there was not a single person among the people less than harmful."
34451,"(34451) I heard Abu Bakr; Omar favored them, giving some of them two thousand, and some of them six hundred."
34452,"(34452) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash mentioned; In his saying: {Then God will bring a people whom He will love and who will love Him}, he said: The people of Al-Qadisiyah."
34453,"(34453) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Saad, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Utba, who said: Omar wrote to Saad. And other princes of Kufa: As for what comes after, there has come to me between Al-Athib and Helwan, and that is sufficient for you. If you fear Allah and make peace, He said: And He wrote: Put a battle between you and the enemy."
34454,"(34454) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, who said: A man passed by on the Day of Qadisiyah. His stomach, or his back, had been torn apart. He said to some of those who passed by him: Join me from him. Come close to the point of a spear, or two spears. For the sake of God, he said: So he passed by him, and he did so."
34455,"(34455) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I saw the companions of slaves drinking Al-Qadisiyah wine. Among them is Amr bin Maymun."
34456,"(34456) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of some of his companions, who said: Talha ibn Ubaid Allah bought a land from Nashastuj, Nashastuj of Banu Talha, this is the one with the two weapons. Omar came and mentioned that to him, and he said: I am You bought amazing land. Omar said: Who did you buy it from? Who are the people of Kufa? Did you buy it from the people of Al-Qadisiyah? Talhah said: How did you buy it from all the people of al-Qadisiyah? He said: You did not make anything. Faye"
34457,"(34457) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of whomever he mentions; The people of Qadisiyah oppressed the foreigners until they fought for three days."
34458,"(34458) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Umayla, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: A man from the people of Kufa and a man from the people of the Levant disagreed and they bragged, so the Kufay said: We are the Companions of the Day Al-Qadisiyah, and on such-and-such a day, and the Levantine said: We are the companions of the Day of Yarmouk, such-and-such and such-and-such a day. Thus, Hudhayf said: Both of you did not witness God. Ad and Thamud perished, and God did not conspire with them when He destroyed them, and there is no village more worthy of repaying a large land than it, meaning Kufa."
34459,"(34459) Affan told us, he said: Abu Awani told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Riyah, on the authority of his father; They found a grave in the cities and found in it a man wearing clothes woven with gold, and they found money with him. So they brought it to Ammar bin Yasser, and he wrote about it to Omar bin Al-Khattab, and Omar wrote to him: I should give it to them, but no. You snatch it away."
34460,"(34460) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah; Omar appointed Al-Sa'ib ibn Al-Aqra' to rule over Al-Mada'in, and while he was in his session, he brought a statue of zero as if it were A man said, “This is what God has in his hand,” and he spread out his hand and clenched some of his fingers, and said: This is for me, this is from what God has bestowed. Ali, so he wrote about it to Omar, and Omar said: You are one of the Muslims’ workers, so put it in the treasury of the Muslims."
34461,"(34461) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of al-Nu’man bin Hamid; Ammar took some spoils, divided some of them, and wrote to Omar apologizing to consult him. He said: He will pledge allegiance to the people until the rider arrives."
34462,"(34462) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Shibl bin Awf: He was from the people of Al-Qadisiyah. And he was combing his beard."
34463,"(34463) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Milhan bin Sulaiman bin Tharwan, who said: Salman was an emir. Al-Mada'in, when it was Friday, he said: O Zaid, arise and remind your people."
34464,"(34464) Affan told us, he said: Abu Hilal told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, he said: Ali Ibn Umm Maktum was on the day Al-Qadisiyah is a shining shield."
34465,"(34465) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Saad and I disagreed. In Al-Qadisiyah in wiping over the socks."
34466,"(34466) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidiya, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A man fled from Al-Qadisiyah. Or Muharran, or some of those scenes. Then Omar came and said: I have perished. I fled, and Omar said: No, I am your group."
34467,"(34467) Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Al-Walid narrated to us, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, he said: I met two thousand The Banu Asad witnessed Al-Qadisiyah in two thousand, and their banners were in the hands of Sammak, the owner of the mosque."
34468,"(34468) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Asim al-Ahwal, who said: Subaih asked Abu Uthman al-Nahdi while I was listening: He said to him: Have you met the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, I greeted him at the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I gave him three alms, but I did not meet him, and I fought During the era of Omar, I witnessed the conquest of Qadisiyah, Jalula, Tustar, Nayavand, Yarmouk, and Azerbaijan. And Mihran, and Rustum, we used to eat ghee and leave the wood, so I asked him about the circumstances? They said: We were not asked about it, meaning the food of the polytheists.
(Ibn Saad 97 Musnad 628)"
34469,"(34469) Aidh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He was struck on the Day of Al-Qadisiyah. The slaves were struck by their arrows as they were struck by the free men."
34470,"(34470) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: When the delegation of Al-Qadisiyyah came, he detained them. For three days, He did not give them permission, then He gave them permission. He said: You say: We met and defeated us. Rather, it is Allah who defeated and conquered."
34471,"(34471) Abu Usama told us, he said: Al-Salt bin Bahram told us, he said: Jam’ bin Umair Al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abd Allah Ibn Omar said: I saw a group of young men, so I bought some of the spoils for forty thousand, so I brought them to Omar, and he said: What is this? I said: I bought the spoils for forty thousand. He said: O Safiyyah, keep what Abdullah bin Omar brought with him. I have determined for you. To take something out of it, she said: O Commander of the Faithful, even if it is not good? He said: That is for you.
 He said: So he said to Abdullah bin Omar: What do you think, if I were taken to Hell, would I be ransomed? I said: Yes, even if I have power over everything.
 He said: It is as if I witnessed you on the day of Jalawla while you were pledging allegiance, and they said: This is Abdullah bin Omar, the companion of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the son of the Commander of the Faithful, and the most generous of his family to him, and so are you. He said: If They will make concessions to you by a hundred, which is more preferable to them than to exorbitate you for a dirham, and I am an apportioner, and I will give you of the profit. The best thing a man earns from Quraysh is, I will give you the profit of a dirham for a dirham. He said: So he left me for seven days, then he called the merchants. So he sold it for four hundred thousand, and he gave me eighty thousand, and he sent for three hundred thousand and twenty thousand to Saad, and he said: Divide this money among those who witnessed the event, and if one of them dies, then send his share to his heirs. (Abu Ubaid 636)"
34472,"(34472) Abu Al-Muwari’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: When Sa’d conquered Jalawla, the Muslims were attacked by a thousand thousand, he divided. For a horseman, three thousand mithqals, and for a footman, a thousand mithqals."
34473,"(34473) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Saad told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar came. With spoils from the spoils of Jalawla, including gold and silver, so he began to divide them among the people, then a son of his came, called: Abd. The Most Gracious, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful, give me a ring. He said: Go to your mother to give you something to drink from a stalk. He said: By God, he did not give me anything."
34474,"(34474) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Hisham bin Saad told us, he said: Zayd bin Aslam told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Arqam, owner of the Muslims’ treasury, saying to Omar bin Al-Khattab: O Commander of the Faithful, we have One of the jewels of Jalawla, and vessels of gold and silver. He saw your opinion about it and said: If you see me empty, let me know. Then he came one day and said: I see you today empty, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: Extend a bow for me in the bridge. So he spread out a bowl for him, then he brought that money, so he poured it over him, and he came and stood over him, then he said: Oh God, you have mentioned this. Money, so you said: {beautiful to the people is the love of lusts, such as women and children, and hoarded hoards of gold and silver} and you said: {so that you may not grieve over what has befallen you, nor rejoice in what you have given us} Oh God, we cannot help but rejoice in what you have adorned for us. Oh God, spend it in a rightful way, and I seek refuge in You from its evil."
34475,"(34475) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Samurah ibn Ja’un. Al-Amiriyy said: I found a cloak woven with gold from brocade on the day of Jalawla, so I wanted to sell it, so I threw it on my shoulders. So I passed by Abdullah bin Omar, and he said: Do you sell cloaks? I said: Yes, he said: How much? I said: For three hundred dirhams. He said: Your garment is not equal to that, and if you wish, I can take it. I said: You may wish. He said: So he took it."
34476,"(34476) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Hayyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: Omar came from Jalawla’ with six thousand thousand, so the gift was obligatory."
34477,"(34477) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus bin Ubad Allah told us, he said: Al-Hakam bin Al-Araj told us, he said: I asked Ibn Omar about wiping over the socks? He said: Saad and I disagreed about that while we were in Jalawla."
34478,"(34478) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Waqa’ bin Iyas al-Asadi, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, who said: We were with Salman in Ghaza, either in Jalula'ah, or in Nawand, he said: A man passed by who had gathered some fruit, so he divided it among His companions, then Salman passed by and insulted him. He replied to Salman, and he did not know him. He said: So it was said: This is Salman. He said: So he returned to Salman. He apologized to him, he said: Then the man said to him: What is permissible for us among the people of the people of Dhimma, O Abu Abdullah? He said: Three; From your blindness to your guidance, and from your poverty to your riches, and when you accompany a friend among them, you eat from his food, and he eats from Your food, and riding your animal so that you do not turn it away from the direction of your desire."
34479,"(34479) Muawiyah bin Amr told us, he said: Zayed told us, he said: Asim bin Kulayb Al-Jarmi told us, he said: My father told me; That he delayed the news of Nahavand and Ibn Muqrin to Umar, and that he was seeking victory, and that the people were seeing who Al-Istansirah said that there was no mention of him except Nahawand and Ibn Muqrin. He said: Then a Bedouin came to them and said: What We reported to you on the authority of Nahavand and Ibn Muqrin. They said: What is that? He said: Nothing, he said: So I went to Omar, he said: So he sent for him, and he said: What did Nayavand and Ibn Muqrin mention of you? If you bring news, tell us. He said: O Commander of the Faithful, I am So-and-so, the son of So-and-so, I left with my family and property, migrating to God and His Messenger. Until we stopped at such-and-such a place, then when we set out, behold, there was a man on a red camel, the like of whom I have never seen, so we said: Where did you come from? He said: From Iraq. We said: What did the people tell? He said: They met, so God defeated the enemy, and Ibn Muqrin was killed. And no, by God, I do not know what happened. Neither Nawand nor Ibn Muqrin said: Do you know which day of Jumu’ah it is? He said: No, by God, I do not know. He said: But I know. So he counted your places of residence. He said: We set out on such-and-such a day, and we camped in such-and-such a place. So he counted his places of residence. He said: That. On the day of such-and-such a gathering, perhaps you will have encountered hail from the hail of the jinn, for they have hail. He said: So it passed. God willing, then the news came that they met on that day."
34480,"(34480) Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, he said: He delayed news of Omar. Nayavand told Numan, so he asked for help."
34481,"(34481) Abu Usama told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Mudrak bin Awf Al-Ahmasi He said: While I was with Omar when the messenger of Al-Numan bin Muqrin came to him, and Omar asked him about the people? He said: Then they mentioned to Omar those who were injured on the day of Nayavand, and they said: So-and-so and so-and-so were killed, and others we do not know, so Omar said: But God knows them. They said: And a man who sold himself, meaning Awf bin Abi Hayyya, Abu Shubail Al-Ahmasi, and he said Mudarrak bin Awf: By God, he is my uncle, O Commander of the Faithful. People claim that he threw himself into destruction with his own hands. Omar said: Those people lied, but he was one of those who bought the afterlife for this world. Ismail said: He was injured while fasting. So he endured and had a breath, but he refused to drink until he died."
34482,"(34482) Abu Asama told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: I came to Omar An-Numan bin Muqrin was mourning, so he placed his hand on his head and began to cry."
34483,"(34483) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah, he said: I sat with Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and he said: I I remember Omar bin Al-Khattab when he mourned Al-Numan bin Muqrin."
34484,"(34484) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mahdi bin Maimun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Yaqoub told us. On the authority of Bishr ibn Shaghaf, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salam, he said: When Nahavand was conquered, the Muslims captured captives from Captives of the Jews. He said: And the head of Goliath came to redeem the captives of the Jews. He said: And he wounded a man of the Muslims. My maid, Busra, in the morning. He said: He came to me and said: Would you please walk with me to this man? Perhaps he would value me. With this maid? He said: So I went with him, and an arrogant old man who had a translator came in and said to his translator: Ask this maid. Will he agree? Ali, this Arab? He said: And I saw him being jealous when he saw her beauty. He said: He told her with his tongue, so she understood what he said, so I said to him: She sinned because of what was in her. Your book of asking this slave girl about what was behind her clothes, and he said to me: You lied, you will not know what is behind her clothes. My book? I said: I know your book more than you. He said: You know more about my book than me? I said: I know your book better than you. He said: Who is this? They said: Abdullah bin Salam. He said: So I left that day.
 He said: So he sent a messenger to me with the intention that you come to me. He said: And he sent to me an animal, saying: So I set out for him, for the life of God. Out of hope that he would be safe, he detained me with him for three days. I would read the Torah to him and he would make you cry. He said: And I said: To him: Indeed, by God, he is the Prophet whom you find in your book. He said: So he said to him: What should I do with the Jews? He said: I told him: The Jews will not avail you at all before God. He said: Misery overcame him and he refused to be converted to Islam. (Bukhari 3159)"
34485,"(34485) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abu Imran al-Junai told us, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Abd Allah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Maqil bin Yassar; Omar bin Al-Khattab consulted with Al-Hurmuzan in Persia, Isbahan, and Azerbaijan, and he said: Isbaan is the head, and Persia And Azerbaijan has two wings. If you cut off one of the wings, the head attaches to the other wing, and if you cut the head, the two wings fall into place. So he started with the head, and entered the mosque, and saw Al-Numan bin Muqrin praying, so he sat next to him, and when he finished his prayer He said: I only saw your employer. He said: As for a collector, no, but a raider. He said: You are a raider. So he directed him and wrote to me. May the people of Kufa extend his support. He said: And with him were Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam, Amr bin Maadi Karib, Hudhayf, Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba, and Ibn Omar. And Al-Ash'ath bin Qais.
 He said: So Al-Nu’man sent Al-Mughaira bin Shu’ba to their king, and he is called the one with the eyebrows, so he informed them He showed them, and it was said to those with eyebrows: Indeed, the Messenger of the Arabs is here. So he consulted with his companions and said: What do you see? Should I sit for him in the glory of kingship and the setting of kingship, or should I sit for him in the setting of war? They said: No, but sit for him in the glory of the kingdom, so he sat on his bed.He placed the crown on his head, and the kings’ sons sat on thrones, wearing gold and brocade earrings and bracelets. He said: So he gave permission for the raider, so two men took the hyena, and with him his spear and sword, he said: So he began to stab him with his spear. He spread their rugs to make them fly, until he stood in front of him, saying: So he began to speak to him, and the interpreter was interpreting. Between them: You Arabs have been afflicted with hunger and hardship, and you have come. If you wish, we can meet you and return.
 He said: Then Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba spoke, and he thanked God and praised Him, then he said: We Arabs were humiliated by him. We have intercourse with people, but we do not intercourse with them, and we eat dogs and carrion. Indeed, God has sent a prophet from among us, in honor from us. He has bestowed upon us according to And we believed in a hadith, which said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent with what he was sent with, and he informed us of the things we found. Just as He said, “And indeed, He promised us, in what He promised us, ‘We will possess what is here and overcome it,’ and indeed, I see that our Lord is distinguished.”"
34486,"(34486) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Habib bin Al-Shahid, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: When Al-Nu’man carried, He said: By God, we had not stepped on his shoulders until he was attacked among the people."
34487,"(34487) Shazan narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Junai, on the authority of Alqamah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Maqil bin Yassar said: He consulted Omar al-Hurmuzan, then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Affan, except that he said: Then al-Nu’man came to them. Banawand, and between them and between them was a river. So Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah sent him away, and he crossed the river to them and made them king. On that day he will be the one with the eyebrows."
34488,"(34488) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said: Asbat bin Nasr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abd Khair, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ Ibn Khuthaym, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Salam; An old Jewish man fell for him, so he passed by the head of the Goliath and said: O head of the Goliath, you will buy from this. The slave girl? So they spoke to her, and behold, he was religious. He said: How much? He said: For four thousand. He said: I have no need for it, so Abdullah bin Salam swore: He will not decrease it, so Abdullah bin Salam left. Something, so he recited these verses: {And if they come to you as captives, you will ransom them}, so Abdullah bin Salam said: You? He said: Yes. He said: To buy it, or to get out of your debt. He said: I have taken it. He said: So grant me whatever you wish. He said: So he took two thousand from him, and returned two thousand to him."
34489,"(34489) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awani narrated to us, he said: Dawud bin Abdullah Al-Awdi narrated to me, on the authority of Hamid bin Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari; That a man who was called: Hamma, one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Asbaan, fighting in Omar disagreed with him, and said: Oh God, his friend claims that he would love to meet you, so if his friend is truthful, then support him with his truthfulness. And if he is lying, then resolve it against him, and if he hates it, O God, do not turn away his lava from this journey of his. He said: So he took it. Death. He died in Isbahan. He said: Then Abu Musa stood up and said: O people, by God, have we not heard what we have heard from? Your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and nothing has reached our knowledge except that his fever is a witness."
34490,"(34490) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: We besieged the city of Nayavand. So I gave Mu`adid a garment of mine and he used it to wear it, then a stone hit him in the head, so he started wiping it and looking at me and saying: Indeed, it is a small one, and God blesses the small one."
34491,"(34491) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Silt, and Abu Musafa’, He said: Omar bin Al-Khattab wrote to us while we were with Al-Numan bin Muqrin: If you meet the enemy, do not flee, and if you gain spoils, do not exaggerate. When we met the enemy, Al-Nu’man said to the people: Do not come to blows with them. That was on the day of its gathering, until the Commander of the Faithful had ascended. The pulpit was asking for victory. He said: Then We confronted them, so An-Nu`man was shortened, and said: They imprisoned me as a garment, and go to your enemy, and do not Were we of you? He said: Then God granted us victory. He said: And the news came to Umar. Al-Numan and so-and-so and so-and-so and men we do not know were injured, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: But God knows them."
34492,"(34492) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq, saying: I heard Abu Malik and Abu Musafa from Two beautiful hadiths; Verily, Omar’s letter came to you with Al-Nu’man bin Muqrin Banawand: As for what follows, perform the prayer at its appointed time, and when you meet the enemy, do not Flee, and if you are victorious, do not go to extremes."
34493,"(34493) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, who said: Umar wrote to al-Nu’man ibn Muqrin: Seek advice and seek help. In your war with your gun, Amr bin Maadi is in distress, and do not give them anything of the matter, for every craftsman knows best. With his industry"
34494,"(34494) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: Al-Nu’man bin Muqrin was in charge of the army of the people of Al-Kufa and Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari over the soldiers of the people of Basra."
34495,"(34495) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: We invaded Balanjar with Salman bin Rabi’a. So He made it difficult for us to carry the animals of the spoils, and made it easy for us to use the sieve, the rope, and the sieve."
34496,"(34496) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn al-Asbaani, on the authority of al-Shaybani, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Malik ibn Suhar, who said: We attacked Balanjar and my brother was injured. He said: So I carried him behind me, and Hudhayf saw me and said: Who is this? So I said: My brother was injured, we will come back and open it, God willing. Hudhafi said: No, by God, he will never open it to me, nor Constantinople, nor Daylam."
34497,"(34497) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Malik ibn Suhar, he said: We invaded Balanjar, but they did not open it, so they said: We will go back and open it, so Hudhafi said: Do not open this, nor the city of disbelief. Nor Daylam, except for a man from the family of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace."
34498,"(34498) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’, and Muhammad bin Suqi, on the authority of Al-Sha’biy, who said: When Salman invaded Balanjar, he struck He divided a bundle of musk, and when he returned, his wife entrusted it to him. When he fell ill, the one in which he died fell ill, and he said to his wife And as he died, he said, “Show me the bag that I entrusted you with,” and she brought it to him. He said, “Bring me a clean vessel,” and she brought it. He said: Add it, then sacrifice it around me, for it is a creation of God’s creation that will come to me. They do not eat food, but they find The wind, then he said: Get out of me and treat me, so I left, then came back and he had finished."
34499,"(34499) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of his father, he said: We were with Salman. Ibn Rabi`a in Balanjar, and I saw the crescent of Shawwal on the twenty-nineth day of the thirty-fifth night. He said: So he said: Show him, and I showed him, so he ordered the people to break their fast."
34500,"(34500) Ibn Idris told us, he said: He heard his father and uncle mention it. He said: Salman said: I killed this hundred with my sword. All of them worship other than Allah. I have not killed a patient man among them."
34501,"(34501) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: It is not opened. Constantinople, nor Daylam, nor Tabaristan, except a man from Banu Hashim."
34502,"(34502) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Mujalid, who said: He made peace with all the people of the mountain, and nothing was taken from the mountain. Forcefully"
34503,"(34503) Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Mutarrif, who said: Anything above the color of light is black, and anything below the color of black is black. Fay’, he said: This blackness of ours is Fay’."
34504,"(34504) Shazan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, he said: I was among those He conquered Tikrit, and we made an agreement with them that they would show us a market, and we made them safe. He said: So they showed us a market. He said: So he was killed. A certain number of them, then their leader came and said: You have made for us the protection of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the protection of Amir The believers, and I protected you, then you betrayed them? Then our emir said: If you present just witnesses against his killer, we will lead you with it, and if you wish, you can swear and we will give it to you. Blood money, and if you wish, we will swear to you and will not give you anything. He said: So they made appointments for the morrow, and they came, and their pastor came, and he thanked God and praised Him, then he mentioned the heavens and the earth, and whatever he wanted. May God even mention the Day of Resurrection, then He said: The first thing He will begin with of blood disputes is blood feuds. He said: Then the son of Adam disputes, and his companion is judged for him, then the first is taken, then the first, until the matter ends with our companion. And your friend, he said: Then it will be said to him: Why did you kill me? He said: We do not like for your friend to have an argument against our friend, for him to say: Your family has taken your blood money after you."
34505,"(34505) Qarad Abu Nuh narrated to us, he said: Othman bin Muawiyah Al-Qurashi narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Early, he said: When Abu Musa came with the people to Al-Hurmuzan and those with him in concealment, he said: They established a Sunnah, or something similar, not They will be sincere with him. He said: Al-Hurmuzan had killed a man from among their tribes and nobles, so his brother set off until he came. Abu Musa, and he said: What will you do for me if I direct you to the entrance? He said: Ask me whatever you want. He said: I ask you to spare my blood and the blood of my family, and to keep distance between us and what is in it. Our hands of our wealth and our dwellings. He said: Then that is yours. He said: Seek for me a wise man with a mind and a heart who will bring you a matter. Clearly
 He said: So Abu Musa sent for Majza’ bin Thawr Al-Sadusi and said to him: Find a man from your people who is a man of wisdom and heart. And he is not in any danger, for if he is afflicted, his affliction will be easy for the Muslims, and if he is safe, he will come steadfast, for I do not know. He did not bring this trick, and I do not believe in him or trust him.
 He said: He said: Partial: I have found. He said: Who is he? So bring him. He said: I am he. Abu Musa said: May God have mercy on you. This is what I wanted, so seek a man.He said: So he said: Mujza’ bin Thawr: By God, I will not baptize an old woman from Bakr bin Wa’il. I will ransom the son of Umm Mujza’ with her son. He said: If you refuse, then it will be easy.
 So he put on white clothes, took a handkerchief, and took with him a dagger, then he went to the storeroom until he swam and passed on to... Medina, so he entered it at the entrance to the water, where he entered upon the people of Medina. He said: So he entered it at a severe entrance. Sometimes it is so narrow that he lies on his stomach, and sometimes it expands so that he walks upright, and sometimes he crawls until He entered Medina and Abu Musa ordered him to remember the way to the gate of Medina, the way to the wall, and the place of Al-Hurmuzan, so he set off with it. Al-Dakhan until he showed him the way to the wall and the way to the door, then he set off with him to the house of Al-Hurmuzan, and Abu Musa had instructed him. Do not precede me in any matter.
 When he saw Al-Hurmuzan sitting and around him, I tickled him while he was drinking, and he said to the Al-Dhaqan: This is Al-Hurmuzan? He said: Yes. He said: This is the one from which the Muslims encountered what they encountered. But by God, I will give them relief from it. He said: Then the Deaqan said to him: No. do,They are guarding and blocking you from entering this entrance, but he refused to do so except to go on. Al-Dhaqan told him to kill Al-Alaj, so Al-Dhaqan told him to stop killing him, but he refused, so Al-Dhaqan mentioned what his father had said. Musa told him: Beware that you do not precede me in a matter. So he said: Has your companion not commanded you not to precede him in a matter? He said: Ah, by God, had it not been for this, I would have given them some relief from it. So he returned with Al-Daqqan to his abode, and stayed for the rest of the day. In the evening, then he returned to Abu Musa, so Abu Musa delegated the people with him, so he sent three hundred and more, so he ordered them to wear The man had two garments, nothing more, and a sword. So the people did so. He said: They sat on the bank of the river, waiting for his part. He came to them, and he was with Abu Musa, giving him a will and ordering him. Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakra said: And they do not have the right to do so. There is something else, referring to death, so I will see what it does, while the table was placed in the hands of Abu Musa. He said: It was as if he was ashamed not to eat anything from the table. He said: So he ate some grapes and ate them, but he was not able to eat them. He took it slowly, then threw it under the tent, and Abu Musa bade him good-bye and entrusted him, so he said its reward to my father. Musa: I ask you for something, so give it to me.He said: Do not ask me for anything unless I give it to you. He said: So give me your sword and I will take it to my sword. So he called for his sword for him. So he gave it to him.
 So he went to the people while they were waiting for him until he was among them, so he said the takbir and fell into the water, and all the people fell. He said: Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakra says: It is as if they were ducks, so they swam until they passed, then he set off with them to the Negev, which Water entered from it, so he said “Allahu Akbar”, then he entered, and when he reached Medina, he looked and saw that there were no people with him, except thirty-five. Or thirty-six men, so he said to his companions: Shall I not return to them and let them in? Then a man from the people of Kufa, who is called a coward because of his courage, said: Someone else, let him say this. It will only suffice. You are upon yourself, so proceed as you are commanded to do. He said to him: You have been injured. So he went with a group of them to the door and placed them on him. He went with his group to the wall, and he went with those who remained until he climbed to the wall, and some of his bracelets descended on him, and with him was a meteorite. So he stabbed his part, but he confirmed it, and his part said to them: Go about your affairs, let nothing distract you from him, so they attacked him. Paradise, so that they would know his location, and they went on and the Muslims said the takbir on the wall and at the gate of the city.They opened the door and the Muslims approached as was their custom until they entered Medina. It was said to Hormuzan: These Arabs have entered. He said: There is no doubt that they trampled on them. He said: Where did they enter from? He was secure in the heavens, he said: and he fortified himself in his reeds. Then Abu Musa came galloping on his Arab horse, until he entered upon Anas bin Malik while he was with the people, and he said: But we O Abu Hamza, we did not do anything today, and they have finished with the people. They killed those they killed, captured those they captured, and marched around. With Ramadan, with his reed, but they did not reach him until they were safe from him, and the ruling of Omar bin Al-Khattab, the Commander of the Faithful, came down to him. He said: So Abu Musa sent them with Anas with Al-Hurmuzan and his companions, and they set out with them until they came to Omar. He said: So he sent for him. Anas: What do you think of these people? Bring them in naked and bound, or I will command them and they take their finery and uniform. He said: Then Omar sent to him You brought them in, as you say, naked and wrapped, for no more than being a treatment, but you brought them in as their adornment. And their uniform until the Muslims knew what God had bestowed upon them. So he commanded them, so they took their uniform and their jewelry until they entered upon Ali. Omar,Al-Hurmuzan said to Omar: O Commander of the Faithful, what words should I say to you? The words of a living man who lives on, or the words of a murdered man? He said: Then she came out of the age of saying something that he did not return. He spoke, and there is no harm to you. Then Al-Hurmuzan said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, You know how we were and how you were, when we were all astray. The Arab tribes used to see each other as rivals. Our bracelets, so they would flee the distant land. But when God guided you and was with you, we were not able to fight him, so Anas returned with them.
 In the evening, Omar sent a message to Anas, saying: “Come upon me with your captives in the morning, and I will behead them.” Anas came to him and said: By God, O Omar, what is that? No, he said: Why? He said: You said to the man: Speak, there is no harm to you. He said: You will bring me proof of this, or I will make you worse. He said: Anas asked the people who were sitting with Omar, and he said: Didn’t Omar say to the man, “Speak, there is nothing wrong with you?” They said: Yes, he said: So that was difficult for Omar, he said: Either no, so he took them away from me and took them to a village, which is said to be: He pushed you into the sea, and when they headed toward them, Omar raised his hand and said: Oh God, break it with them as three, so they boarded the ship. Then it hit them and broke, and it was close to the ground, so they came out.Then a Muslim man said: If he had called for them to be drowned, they would have drowned, but he only said: break it with them. He said: so he made them endure."
34506,"(34506) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Anas: He said: We were besieged and concealed, so Al-Hurmuzan descended upon the judgment of Omar. So Abu Musa sent him with me, and when we came to Omar, Al-Hurmuzan remained silent and did not speak, so Omar said to him: Speak, and he said: Talk. Living or dead words? He said: Speak, there is no problem. He said: We and you Arabs, as long as God leaves us and you alone, we would kill you. And we excluded you, but when God was with you, we had no hand over you. Omar said: What do you say, Anas? I said: O Commander of the Faithful, I left behind me a strong thorn and many people who, if I were to kill them, would be hopeless of life. And he was more severe in their piety, and if she was shy, the greed of the people would please her.
 He said: O Anas, the one who killed Al-Bara’ bin Malik and Majza’ bin Thawr was ashamed, so when I feared that he would attack him, I said: Not. Until Sabil killed him, then Omar said: Why? Did he give you? Did you catch him? I said: I did not do it, but you said to him: Speak, there is no problem. He said: You will bring me someone who will bear witness, or I will begin your punishment. So I left him, and behold, I was with Al-Zubair. He had memorized what I had memorized, and he testified with him, so he left him, and Al-Hurmuzan surrendered and departed. No"
34507,"(34507) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Habib bin Shihab, on the authority of his father; He attacked with Abu Musa until the day came when they provided cover. The Ash'arite was shot and struck, so I stood up behind him with shield until... He regained consciousness. He said: I was the first Arab man to light a fire in a hidden gate. He said: Then when we conquered it and took the captives, Abu Musa said: Choose ten soldiers from among the soldiers to be with you during this captivity, until we bring you. Then he went on after that through the land. Until they conquered what they had conquered of the two lands, then they returned to him, and Abu Musa divided the spoils among them, and he used to give the knight Two shares, and the man gets one share, and he did not differentiate between the woman and her children when selling."
34508,"(34508) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Habib bin Shihab, he said: My father told me, he said: I was the first to light the fire. At the gate of cover, Al-Ash'ari was shot and killed. When they conquered it and took the captives, he appointed me as commander over ten of my people, and sent a man to me. Equity my arrows and horse arrows before the spoils."
34509,"(34509) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Al-Awwam ibn Muzahim, on the authority of Khaled ibn Sihan, he said: She witnessed Four or five women covered themselves with Abu Musa, and they were to give water to drink and treat the wounded, so Abu Musa contributed to them."
34510,"(34510) Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Malik; He said: I witnessed Fath Tustar with Al-Ash’ari. He said: So we infected Daniel with the lice. He said: So the people of the lice were when they became evil. They took him out and drew water with him, and We brought with him sixty sealed jars. He said: So We opened a jar from the bottom of it, and a jar from the bottom. The middle of it, and he drew it from the farthest part, and we found in each jar ten thousand. Hammam said: I did not see it. He said only ten thousand. And We brought with him two scraps of linen, and We brought with him a quarter in which was a book, and he was the first man upon whom a man fell. Balanbar, it is called: Harqus. He said: So the Ash’arite gave him the two ribatas, and he gave him two hundred dirhams. He said: Then he asked After that, he refused to return them to him and divided them into turbans among his companions.
 He said: There was with us a Christian worker named Naim, and he said: With your help, this quarter of what is in it. They said: If not Whether there is gold, or silver, or the Book of God in it, he said: For what is in it is the Book of God, so they thought that They sold him the book, so we sold him a quarter for two dirhams and gave him the book. His qatadah said: Then he refused to sell it. The Qur’an, because Al-Ash’ari and his companions disliked selling that book.
 Hammam said: Farqad al-Sabkhi claimed that he said: Abu Tamimah told me; Omar wrote to Al-Ash’ari: To wash Daniel with Sidr and basil water, and to pray over him, for he is a Prophet. He called on his Lord that there would be no one to follow him except the Muslims."
34511,"(34511) Shazan narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Juniy, on the authority of Anas; When they opened the cover, he said: We found a man whose nose was a cubit in the coffin. They were demonstrating, or raining rain on him. So Abu Musa wrote to Omar bin Al-Khattab about this, and Omar wrote: This is one of the prophets, and fire does not consume. Prophets or the earth does not eat prophets. So he wrote to him: “Look, you and a man from among your companions,” meaning my father’s companions. Musa, so bury him in a place that no one knows except you. He said: So I and Abu Musa went and buried him."
34512,"(34512) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Habib Abi Yahya; Khalid bin Zayd, whose eye was affected by a mite, said: We besieged its city, and we met a soldier, and the commander of the army Abu Musa, and Al-Dakhan took his covenant and the covenant of those with him, so Abu Musa said: Isolate them, so he proceeded to isolate them, and Abu Musa made He says to his companions: I hope that God will deceive him about himself, so he isolates them and remains the enemy of God, so Abu Musa commanded him to do so. So he called and gave him a lot of money, but he refused and beheaded him."
34513,"(34513) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Habib Abi Yahya, on the authority of Khalid bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Musa, In the same way"
34514,"(34514) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, that he said: I witnessed Fath Tastari with Al-Ash’ari. He said: I did not perform the Fajr prayer until the middle of the day, and I was not pleased with that entire worldly prayer."
34515,"(34515) Rayhan bin Saeed told us, he said: Marzuq bin Amr told me, he said: Abu Farqad told me, he said: We were with Abu Musa, on the day we opened the market of Ahwaz, one man from the polytheists ran hard and two men from the Muslims ran after him, he said: So between us He is striving and they are striving, when one of them said to him: He is shielded, so the man got up and they took him and brought him to Abu Musa, and Abu Musa He struck the necks of the captives, until the matter came to the man, and one of the two men said: This has made him safe. Abu Musa said: How was security made for him? He said: He was walking across the land, so I told him: What is a shield for him? So he got up. Abu Musa said: What is his shield? He said: Do not be afraid. He said: This is security. He cleared his way. He said: So they cleared the man’s way."
34516,"(34516) Marhum bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sudais Al-Adawi, who said: We invaded with the idiot prince. So we gained victory over them, then we came to Al-Awaz, and there were people of sandals and bracelets, so we fought them hard and gained victory over them. We captured many captives, so we divided them up, and the man struck the head and the two of them, so we fell upon the women, so our emir wrote to Omar. Ibn Al-Khattab, as it was, wrote to him: Indeed, you have no ability to inhabit the land. Leave what is in your hands of the captives. And do not make any of them possess any of them, and impose upon them a tax equal to the amount of land that is in their possession, so we left what was in our possession. Of the captivity, how many of our children were overcome by diarrhea, and among those whom we afflicted were people from the baptism who imitated the Arabs, sparing their beard. And they cover themselves and take shelter in their assemblies. So he wrote about them to Omar, so Omar wrote to him: If I am closer to you than you, then who? He became more peaceful than them, so he joined him to the Muslims. When they were tried with the people, they had no strength against them, and the bracelets were stronger than theirs. So he wrote to Omar among them, so Omar wrote to him: I will bring them closer to you. So whoever of them submits to Islam, join him with the Muslims."
34517,"(34517) Affan told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Muhallab, he said: We were tempted by warnings. And we took advantage of them as if it had been a covenant with them, so Omar wrote: Return what you took from them. He said: They returned, until they returned the women. Pregnancy"
34518,"(34518) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ata bin Al-Sa’ib narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Zur’i bin Amr bin Jarir; That a man was loud and used to speak out against the enemy with Abu Musa, so they took spoils, so Abu Musa gave him his share, but he did not He died, but he refused to take him except all of them, so he struck him with twenty lashes and shaved him, so he collected his hair, and went to Omar, and he entered. Ali, so Jarir said: And I am the closest person to him. So he took out his hair from his shroud and stroked Omar’s chest with it, so he said: By God If it had not been for him, Omar said: He was right, had it not been for the Fire, so he said: What is the matter with you? He said: I was a loud man and used to spite the enemy, so we took spoils and told him about the matter, and he said: He shaved my head and flogged me. Twenty lashes, and he believes that he will not be punished for it, so Omar said: Because all people are as strict as this, he liked it. Of all that was paid to us, he said: Then Omar wrote to Abu Musa: Peace be upon you, but then; So-and-so, the son of so-and-so, told me such-and-such, and I swear to you that if you had done to him what you did in a gathering of people, why If you sat in a group of them, then I will be retaliated against you. And if you did to him what you did in a private group, then sit to him in a private group, and he will be retaliated against you. So the people said to him: Pardon him, and he said: No, by God, I will not leave him to any of the people. So when the letter was given to him, he sat down for retaliation, and he was removed. He raised his head to the heavens and said: I have pardoned him.
 Hammad also said: So Abu Musa gave him some of his shares, and Jarir also said: And I am the closest of people to him. He said: He also said: I have pardoned him for the sake of Allah."
34519,"(34519) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awani narrated to us, he said: Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Simak bin Salamah; When the Muslims conquered a cover, they placed the Muslims’ belongings there and advanced to fight their enemy. He said: Then a curtain of concealment betrayed them. So he heated an oven for them and offered them pork and wine, or an oven. He said: Some of them ate and left. He said: So he offered Ali Nahib bin Al-Harith Al-Dhabi, but he refused and was put in the oven. He said: Then the Muslims returned and besieged the people of Medina. Until they reconciled with Al-Dhaqan, Nayib’s nephew said to his uncle: O uncle, this is the killer of Nayib. He said: O nephew, indeed He has a responsibility. Simak said: He informed me that Omar told him that, so he said: May God have mercy on him, and what is upon him if he had eaten?"
34520,"(34520) Abu Asama told us, he said: Al-Ala’ bin Al-Manhal told us, he said: Asim bin Kulayb Al-Jarmi told us, he said: My father told me, he said: We were besieged by Taj, and over us was a man from Banu Sulaym, called: Mujashi bin Masoud. He said: When we conquered it He said: And I was wearing a tight shirt. He said: So I went to one of the dead people we killed from among the non-Arabs. He said: So I took the shirt of some of them. Those were the dead. He said: And there was blood on him. He said: So I washed him between stones and massaged him until I cleaned him. I dressed him and went in. The village, so I took a needle and thread, and stitched my shirt, and Mujashi’ stood up and said: O people, do not exaggerate any of this. He sewed something and will bring it on the Day of Resurrection, even if it were sewn.
 He said: So I went to that shirt and took it off, and I went to my shirt and started to tear it apart, even by God, my son. I tore up my shirt to prevent the thread from breaking, so I set out with the shirt, needle, and thread that I had I took it from the dividers, then threw it into it, then I had not left the world until I saw them boiling the sacks, so when I said: What is this? They said: Our share of the spoils is more than this."
34521,"(34521) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, who said: When he came to Omar, he opened the cover and cover. From the land of Basra, he asked them: Is there anyone from the West? They said: A man from among the Muslims who joined the polytheists, so we captured him. He said: What? What did you do with it? They said: We killed him. He said: Did you not take him into a house, close the door on him, and feed him a loaf of bread every day? Then you asked him to question him three times, and if he repented, otherwise you would kill him? Then he said: Oh God, I did not witness, nor did I command, nor did I approve when He informed me, or when He informed me."
34522,"(34522) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Muhallab ibn Abi Safar He said: We besieged the city of Ahvaz and conquered it, and there was a mention of peace, so we struck some women and made peace with them, and that was achieved. Omar, so he wrote to us: Take their children and return to them their wives, and he had been reconciling with some of them."
34523,"(34523) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Walid narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Omar bin Muhammad bin Hatib, he said: I heard My grandfather, Muhammad bin Hatib, said: A delegation attacked us to Istakhr, and the knight was assigned to the one sitting."
34524,"(34524) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Kaysan told us, he said: I heard Shuways al-Adawi saying: I invaded Maysan. So I took a female slave captive, and we married her until a letter came from Umar: Return the captives of Maysan that are in your hands, so I returned, but I do not know. Under what condition was it repeated, pregnant or not pregnant? So that it will be more beneficial for their villages, and more abundant for their taxes.
(Abu Ubaid 378)"
34525,"(34525) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, he said: I heard Ayyad al-Ash’ari, he said: I witnessed the Yarmouk. And over us are five princes: Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, Yazid bin Abi Sufyan, Ibn Husna, Khalid bin Al-Walid, and Iyad. This is not Iyad who was narrated by Simak. He said: And Omar said: If there is a fight, then Abu Ubaidah is on you. He said: So we wrote to him: Indeed, death has come upon us, and we sought him. He said: Then he wrote to us: Indeed, your letter has come to me. You seek help from me, and I will direct you to someone who has the greatest victory and has brought an army, so seek help from him, and that Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And the victory on the Day of Badr was less than your number, so when this letter of mine comes to you, fight them, and do not withdraw from me. He said: So we fought them, so we defeated them, and we killed them within four farsakhs. He said: And we gained wealth. He said: So we consulted, so he indicated We are required to give a tithe to each head.
 He said: Abu Ubaidah said: Who will bet me? He said: Then a young man said: I do, if you are not angry. He said: Then he preceded him. He said: I saw the two thorns of Abu Ubaidah jumping, and he He succeeded him on an Arabian horse."
34526,"(34526) Abu Usama told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qais, he said: I saw a man who wanted to buy Himself on the Day of Yarmouk, and a woman was pleading with him, so he said: Refuse this man. If only I knew that what I wanted would happen to her. I have not breathed over it. By God, if I were able, a day would not pass that this man would disappear from his place. He pointed with his hand to a mountain. If you overpower my body, then take it. Qays said: We passed by him, and after that we saw him killed in that battle. The battle"
34527,"(34527) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Mus’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’d bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of the one who narrated to him ; Indeed, no voice stronger than his was heard, while he was under the watch of his son on the day of Yarmouk, and he said: This A day from God’s days. Oh God, send down your victory, meaning Abu Sufyan."
34528,"(34528) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Umayla, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: A man from the people of Kufa and a man from the people of the Levant disagreed, and they bragged, so the Kufay said: We are the Companions of the Day Al-Qadisiyah and such-and-such a day. Al-Shami said: We are the companions of Yarmouk and such-and-such a day."
34529,"(34529) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafli, who said: We witnessed Yarmouk. So Omar received us, and we were wearing brocade and silk, so he ordered us to throw stones at us. He said: So we said: What did he hear about us? He said: So we separated from him and said: He hated our adornment. When he met us, he welcomed us. Then he said: You have come to me in the garb of the people of polytheism. Indeed, God did not approve of brocade and silk for those before you."
34530,"(34530) Hussein bin Muhammad told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I witnessed the Yarmouk. So the people picked grapes and fed them, and they ate, but they did not see any harm in them."
34531,"(34531) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: When Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl converted to Islam, he came to the Prophet May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, and he said: O Messenger of God, by God, I will never leave the position I have taken to obstruct you from the path of God, unless I rise. The like of it is for the sake of God, and I will not abandon any expenditure that will turn me away from the path of God, unless I spend the like of it in the path of God, so when It was the day of Yarmouk that he descended, dismounted, and fought fiercely, and was killed, and seventy-one people were found on him, among his stab wounds. And he beat him and threw him away."
34532,"(34532) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Saad told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, he said: When Abu Ubaidah al-Sham was besieged, along with his companions, and they were struck by a severe struggle, so Umar wrote to him: Peace be upon you. As for what follows: For there was never a hardship but that God brought relief after it, and no hardship would be overcome by ease. And He wrote to Him: {O, O Those who believe, be patient and be steadfast, and be united, and fear God, that you may succeed.} He said: Then Abu Ubaidah wrote to him: Peace, but After that, God said: {Indeed, the life of this world is only play and amusement and adornment and boasting among you and multiplication of wealth and children} Until the last verse, he said: Then Omar came out with the letter of Abu Ubaidah, and read it to the people, and said: O people of Medina, it is only Abu Ubaidah wrote to introduce you and urge you to jihad.
 Zaid said: My father said: I was standing in the market, when a bright people came, who had descended from the second place, among them. Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman: They give good tidings. He said: So I went out and strengthened until I entered upon Omar, and I said: O Commander of the Faithful, give good tidings. With God’s victory and conquest, Omar said: God is Great. Perhaps he would have said, “If only it had been Khalid bin Al-Walid.”"
34533,"(34533) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Ezra bin Qais Al-Bajli; When Omar ibn al-Khattab deposed Khaled ibn al-Walid and appointed Abu Ubaidah over the Levant, Khaled rose and addressed the people, and they thanked God. He praised her, then said: The Commander of the Faithful appointed me as governor of the Levant, and even when it was abundant with honey and honey, he isolated me. And others preferred it, saying: Then a man from among the people rose from below him and said: Be patient, O prince, for this is a trial. He said: So he said Khaled: As for Ibn al-Khattab being alive, no, but if the people are in affliction and affliction, and until a man comes to seek the land In it is that which is not on its land, so it cannot be found."
34534,"(34534) Waki’ told us, he said: Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Omar said, when he heard the words of Khalid bin Al-Walid: I will remove the immortal, and I will remove the two so that they know that it is God who supports his religion, not them."
34535,"(34535) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aslam, the servant of Omar, he said: When we came With Omar al-Sham, he harried his camel and went to relieve himself, so I threw my scalp between the two sections of the saddle, and when he came riding on Al-Farwa We met the people of the Levant receiving Omar, and they began to look, and I began to point to them. He said: Omar says: aspire. Their eyes are on the ships of those who have no manners, who want the ships of non-Arabs."
34536,"(34536) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, who said: When Umar came to the Levant, the people met him while he was riding his camel. They said: O Commander of the Faithful, if you were to ride on a horse, the great people and their faces would meet you. So Omar said: I do not see you. “This is here.” The matter is from here, and he pointed with his hand toward the heavens."
34537,"(34537) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: Bilal came to Omar while he was in the Levant, and around him were princes. The soldiers were sitting, and he said: O Omar, and he said: Here I am Omar, and Bilal said to him: Indeed, you are among these and among God, and not Between you and God is one, so look to your right, and look to your left, and look from before you and from behind you. Those around you, by God, eat nothing but bird meat. Omar said: You are right, by God, I will not arise from this gathering of yours. Until they provided for each Muslim man a mudd of food, and his share of vinegar and oil, and they said: That is for us, oh The Commander of the Faithful, God has expanded provision and increased goodness. He said: So yes."
34538,"(34538) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Aslam, the client of Omar, who said: When Omar came to the Levant, a man came to him. One of the gourmets, and he said: I have prepared food, and I would like you to come so that the people of my land can see my honor upon you and your status. With you, or as he said, and he said: We do not enter these churches, or these stores in which there are pictures."
34539,"(34539) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: When the age of the Levant came, The soldiers came to him wearing an garment, slippers, and a turban, while he was wading into the water with the head of his camel. They said to him: O Amir. The believers, the soldiers and the penguins of the Levant will meet you, and you are in this state. He said: Then Omar said: We are a people whom God has honored with Islam, so you will not We seek glory in others."
34540,"(34540) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, he said: Urwah bin Ruwaym narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: I came to Omar when he came to the Levant, and I found him talking in his tent, so I waited for him in the tent, so I heard him. When he was hungry from his sleep, and he was saying: O God, forgive me for my return from the battle of Sarg, meaning when he returned for The epidemic"
34541,"(34541) Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Asir ibn Amr, who said: When Umar al-Sham came, he brought buds. So he rode on him, and when he shook him, he got off him, then said: May God make you ugly, and curse those who teach you."
34542,"(34542) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, he said: Qais bin Muslim informed me, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, He said: When Omar al-Sham came, he addressed the people, and he said: I do not know of a man whose horse was tall in a crowd of people. He said: Then he brought a boy carrying a lamb. He was struck by the leg of a horse, and Omar said to him: I did not hear what you said yesterday. He said: Yes, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: What did he carry you? What did you do? He said: I saw an empty part of the road. He said: I don’t see you apologizing with an excuse. Two men are taking the blame for this, and they are taking you out of The mosque, so it expands in size? And the people were silent, and none of them would answer him. He said: Then he repeated what he said, and Abu Ubaidah said to him: O Prince. Believers: Do you not see in the faces of the people the hatred that you should disgrace their friend? He said: So he said to the boy’s family: Go with him. So they treated him, and by God, if something were to happen to him, I would give you a punishment. He said: So the boy was healed and may God forgive him."
34543,"(34543) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: It was mentioned to him; Omar returned from the Levant when he heard that there was an epidemic in her, but he did not recognize him, and he said: He was only informed that the female summer woman does not come out in the year, so he returned."
34544,"(34544) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yazid al-Rahbi, and Muhammad al-Khawlani, on the authority of Urwah bin Ruwaym, who said: Omar wrote a letter to Abu Ubaidah and he read it to the people with the collector: From Abdullah Omar, the Commander of the Faithful To Abu Ubaidah: Peace be upon you. As for what follows, no one can carry out the command of God among the people except one who has a prudent mind and is far from strong. People will look at his private parts, but he will not be angry with the truth because of his shame, nor will he fear God’s censure from a blameworthy person, and peace be upon you."
34545,"(34545) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, he said: When Umar al-Sham came, Qamis had wandered around. About his seat; A thick Sunblanese shirt, and he sent it to the owner of a man’s arms, or his family. He said: He washed it, patched it, and sewed it. He brought them to him, and he threw them to him, so Omar took them and touched them, and said: This is soft, so he threw them to him. To him, and said: Throw my shirt to me, for it will make them dry because of the sweat."
34546,"(34546) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abi Suda, on the authority of Abu Maryam, he said: When the age of the Levant came, He came to the Mihrab of David, prayed there, recited Surah S., and when he finished prostrating, he prostrated."
34547,"(34547) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Juwayriyah Al-Jarimi, who said: I was among those who marched to the Levant on the Day of Khazir. So we met, and the wind blew upon them, and they turned back, and We killed them during our evening and night until morning. He said: Then Abraham said, Ibn al-Ashtar means: Yesterday I killed a man, and I smelled a perfume from him, and I saw no one but Ibn Murjanah. his feet and his head to the west, or his head to the east and his feet to the west. He said: So I went and looked, and behold, by God, it was him. Ubaid Allah bin Ziyad."
34548,"(34548) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Wa’il, or Wa’il ibn Alqamiya; Al-Hussein witnessed Karbalaa. He said: Then a man came and said: Is Hussein among you? He said: Who are you? He said: Bring good news of the Fire. He said: Rather, a Forgiving Lord, and an obedient intercessor. He said: Who are you? He said: Ibn Hawiza. He said: Oh God, send him to Hell. He said: So he went and swayed his horse on its legs, and it broke off, and it did not Only his leg was left in the stirrup."
34549,"(34549) Abdo bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; The Qur’an was revealed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he was forty-three years old, and he resided in Mecca for ten years. He spent ten years in Medina, and he died when he was sixty-three years old. (Ibn Saad 191)"
34550,"(34550) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amir bin Saad, on the authority of Jarir; He heard Muawiyah deliver a sermon. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died when he was sixty-three years old, and Abu Bakr, Omar, and I am sixty-three years old. (Muslim 1827. Ahmad 96)"
34551,"(34551) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It was revealed to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was forty years old, then he stayed in Mecca for thirteen years, and he was He spent ten days in Medina, and he was arrested when he was sixty-three years old. (Bukhari 3851, Tirmidhi 3621)"
34552,"(34552) Ismail told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ammar, the client of Banu Hashim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. May God bless him and grant him peace. He is sixty-five years old. (Muslim 1827, Tirmidhi 3650)"
34553,"(34553) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ammar, a client of Banu Hashim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent when he was forty years old, and he resided in Mecca for fifteen years. And ten in Medina, and he was arrested when he was sixty-five years old."
34554,"(34554) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: It was revealed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, when he was forty years old. He stayed in Mecca for ten years, and in Medina for ten years."
34555,"(34555) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: Al-Zubayr converted to Islam when he was sixteen years old, and he did not convert to Islam. He left behind a campaign. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, invaded him and was killed when he was sixty-odd years old."
34556,"(34556) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, died. May peace and blessings be upon him, Abu Bakr, Omar, and Ali, who are sixty-three years old, and Othman, who is the son of Naif, and seventy years of age.
(Ibn Abi Asim 166)"
34557,"(34557) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I gathered the arbitrator on At the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I said to him: What is the ruling? He said: Al-Mufassal. Ghayr Hashim added: He was arrested when I was ten years old."
34558,"(34558) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina. I was ten years old, and he died when I was twenty years old. (Bukhari 5166 and Muslim 1603)"
34559,"(34559) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Muslim bin Mukhlid, he said: I was born when he came The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in Medina, and he was arrested when I was ten years old. (Tabarani 1060)"
34560,"(34560) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sinan bin Salamah al-Hudhali narrated to us, on the authority of his father; His grandfather, Sinan bin Salamah, was born on the day of Hunayn. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for him, and he spit in his mouth. He wiped his face and prayed for blessings upon it."
34561,"(34561) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Salem; Omar died when he was fifty-five years old."
34562,"(34562) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Salim bin Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ma’dan bin Abi Talha. Al-Amri said: Omar, may God have mercy on him, was injured on the fourth Wednesday of Dhul-Hijjah."
34563,"(34563) Abu Asama told us, Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Abu Bakr converted to Islam on the day he converted to Islam. Forty thousand dirhams."
34564,"(34564) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her when she was nine years old, and he died on her behalf when she was eighteen years old."
34565,"(34565) Waki’ narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Amr bin Harith saying: I was in A woman’s stomach on the day of Badr."
34566,"(34566) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I was presented to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace on the day of Uhud when I was fourteen years old, so they looked down upon me, and I appeared to him on the day of the ditch when I was five years old. He rewarded you ten times."
34567,"(34567) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab converted to Islam after Forty men and eleven women."
34568,"(34568) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abu Hamza al-Ansari, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The first to convert to Islam with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Ali. He said: This was mentioned to Abraham but he denied it. That, and he said: Abu Bakr."
34569,"(34569) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Salem, who said: I said to Ibn al-Hanafiyyah: Abu Bakr Were the first people to convert to Islam? He said: No."
34570,"(34570) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The first to demonstrate Islam were seven: the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, and Abu Bakr, and Bilal, and Kabbab, and Sahib, and Ammar, and her name was Umm Ammar, as for the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace, so his uncle prevented him, and as for Abu Bakr, his people prevented him, and the others were taken and put on iron armor. And they fasted in the sun until the effort of every one of them had reached its peak, so they gave them what they asked for, so he came to every man of them. His people threw water into it, then they carried it on their sides, except for Bilal, when it was evening. Abu Jahl came and started cursing and insulting a beautiful woman, then he stabbed her in the kiss. He was the first martyr to be martyred. Islam, except for Bilal, for she was humiliated by God until they were fed up, so they put a rope around his neck, then they ordered Their boys, so they took him to the woods of Mecca, and he started saying: “One, One.”"
34571,"(34571) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: They gave them what they asked for, except for a messenger, so they made them stick together. He appeared with satisfaction until his water was gone."
34572,"(34572) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: Khabab was from The immigrants, and he was among those who would be punished by God."
34573,"(34573) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Kurdous say, “Khabab bin Al-Art converted to Islam sixth.” Six, he had one-sixth of Islam."
34574,"(34574) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: I and Ibn Umar were presented to the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him on the day of Badr, so we looked down upon it, and we witnessed on the day of Uhud."
34575,"(34575) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, who said: Subaih asked Abu Uthman: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: I greeted him at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I gave him three alms, but I did not meet him. (Ibn Saad 97)"
34576,"(34576) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hilal ibn Khabbab, on the authority of Misra Abu Salih, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafla, he said: The authenticator of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us."
34577,"(34577) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and I fought during the succession of Abu Bakr and Omar thirty-three, or forty-three, somewhere between Conquest to secret. (Ahmad 314, Tabarani 8205)"
34578,"(34578) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Salamah ibn Kuhayl, on the authority of Habib al-‘Urani, he said I heard Ali saying: I was the first to pray with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
34579,"(34579) Hussein bin Muhammad al-Tamimi told us, Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, he said: Abu said Bakr to Ali: Did you hate my emirate? He said: No, Abu Bakr said: I was in this matter before you."
34580,"(34580) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, who said: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa, and he was one of the companions of The tree"
34581,"(34581) Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father He said: Abdullah said: You have seen me the sixth of six, and there is no Muslim on earth except us."
34582,"(34582) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Layya’, he said: Zayd ibn Amr al-Ma’afiri narrated to me, saying: I heard Abu Thawr al-Fahmi says: Abd al-Rahman ibn Udays al-Balawi came to us, and he was one of those who pledged allegiance under the tree, so he went up He went to the pulpit and thanked God and praised Him, then he mentioned Othman. Abu Thawr said: So we entered upon Othman while he was besieged, and he said: This is the fourth time in Islam."
34583,"(34583) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Juhayfy, he said: I saw The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and this part of it was white, and Zuhair placed his hand on its neck, it was said to my father Juhayfa: Like, who are you then? He said: Sharpen the arrow and sharpen it."
34584,"(34584) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Abdullah bin Utba contrived. And a man from Hamadan. Al-Hamdani said: Abu Bakr is greater than the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abdullah said: No. Rather, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is greater than Abu Bakr. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died while he was the son of Sixty-three years old, and Abu Bakr died when he was sixty-three years old, and Amer bin Saad Al-Bajli said: I will pay the debt. Between the two of you, Jarir bin Abdullah told me; He was with Muawiyah, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died when he was sixty-three years old. Abu Bakr was killed when he was sixty-three, and Omar was killed when he was sixty-three, and I was fifty-seven years old. (Muslim 1827)"
34585,"(34585) A sheikh of ours narrated to us, saying: I heard Ja’far narrating on the authority of his father. He said: Ali greeted me when he was the son of seven. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested when he was twenty-seven years old, and Ali was killed when he was fifty-seven years old."
34586,"(34586) A sheikh of ours told us, he said: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Amer, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas, or Ibn Abbas was asked: Which people? Was he the first to convert to Islam? He said: Did you not hear Hassan bin Thabit say:
If you remember a complaint from a trustworthy brother
The best human being is the most pious and just.
The second, the next, praiseworthy and glorious.

So remind your brother Abu Bakr of what they did.
Except the Prophet, and he fulfilled what was burdened.
And the first of the people among them to believe the messengers
(Hakim 64. Ibn Asakir 39)"
34587,"(34587) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla speaking, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aakim, who said: The letter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was read to us while I was a young boy: Do not benefit from the dead out of dishonor. And no nerves."
34588,"(34588) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Aoun ibn Abi Juhaif, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger was sent God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was among us a charity, so he took charity from our rich and gave it back to our poor, so I was a boy. I was an orphan and had no money, so he gave me a small amount."
34589,"(34589) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Hisham informed us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. It was revealed to him when he was forty years old, and he resided in Mecca for thirteen years. He lived in Medina for ten years, and he died when he was sixty-three."
34590,"(34590) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Naama, he heard it from Khalid bin Umayr, he said: Utba bin Ghazwan addressed us, He said: You saw me on the seventh of the seventh with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Muslim 2278, Ibn Majah 4156)"
34591,"(34591) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, Sulaiman bin Bilal narrated to us, he said: Rabi’i bin Abi Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent at the head of forty, and he stayed in Mecca ten. And in Medina ten, and he died at the age of sixty. (Muslim 1825. Ahmad 240)"
34592,"(34592) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, he said: I saw Zurr bin Hubaysh coming. He is one hundred and twenty years old, and his beard is disturbed by old age, and I saw Abu Amr Al-Shaibani, and he He lived for nineteen hundred years."
34593,"(34593) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: I saw Zurr ibn Hubaysh in the mosque, his beard shaking. From old age, and he says: I am one hundred and twenty years old."
34594,"(34594) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Shaqiq ibn Salamah said to me: O Suleiman, if you saw me while we were I ran away from Khalid bin Al-Walid on the day of Buzakh, so I fell off the camel and almost broke my neck. If I had died on that day It was fire."
34595,"(34595) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: I heard a brother saying: I was eleven years old at that time. Sunnah"
34596,"(34596) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, he heard Omar saying: Oh God, grant us health. And pardon us."
34597,"(34597) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, he said: There was nothing but purity between Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein."
34598,"(34598) Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ash’ayb narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his leaders, who said: The last of them was death in Medina, Jabir. Ibn Abdullah, the last of them to die in Basra was Anas Ibn Malik, and the last of them to die in Kufa was Abdullah Ibn Abi More fulfilling"
34599,"(34599) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his leaders, that Abu Bakr died when he was the son of five. And sixty years of age, and that Omar was killed when he was fifty-one years old, and that Othman was killed when he was nine years old, or eight years old. And eighty."
34600,"(34600) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Harith bin Dhahir, he said: When Abdullah was mourned to Abu Darda’, he said: He did not leave behind anyone like him."
34601,"(34601) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, he said: Ibn Abbas died, and his guardian was Ibn al-Hanafi."
34602,"(34602) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Hafsa, on the authority of a man called: Abu Kulthum, who said: I heard Ibn al-Hanafiyyah say at Ibn Abbas’s funeral: Today the lord of knowledge died."
34603,"(34603) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ammar, a client of Banu Hashim, who said: We sat with Ibn Abbas in the shade of Al-Qasr, at the funeral of Zayd bin Thabit, said: Today a lot of knowledge has been buried."
34604,"(34604) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: They passed by my father’s funeral. Abd al-Rahman Ali Abi Juhayfah, and he said: He was relieved and he was relieved from it."
34605,"(34605) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abjar, he said: I informed Al-Shu’abi of the death of Abraham, and he said: May God have mercy on him. As for him, he did not leave behind a successor like him. As for him, he was dead and more wise than he was alive."
34606,"(34606) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I informed Al-Hasan of the death of Al-Sha’bi, and he said: May God have mercy on him, and by God, He was part of Islam for a certain place."
34607,"(34607) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar was in the market, and a stone was called to him. Then he let go of his pill and stood up, overcome by wailing."
34608,"(34608) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: I came to Omar with an obituary. Al-Numan bin Muqrin, then he placed his hand on his head and began to cry."
34609,"(34609) A sheikh of ours told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, he said: Abraham perished when he was forty-eight years old. He said: Al-Amash: Saeed bin Jubayr perished when he was forty-six years old."
34610,"(34610) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah, who said: I sat with Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and he said to me: Who are you from? I said: From Mazina. He said: I remember the day Omar bin Al-Khattab Al-Numan mourned on the pulpit."
34611,"(34611) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Malik bin Anas told us, on the authority of Salim Abi Al-Nadr, he said: When he died Saad, Aisha ordered him to pass by her and ask forgiveness for him."
34612,"(34612) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, who said: I recited the Qur’an after Your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died twenty years old."
34613,"(34613) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: I have reached eighty years of age and I am as afraid as I am of women."
34614,"(34614) Affan told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hamid, he said: Abu Uthman said: It came to me about thirty and a hundred people. age"
34615,"(34615) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Hajjaj bin Abi Zainab told us, he said: I heard Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, He says: In pre-Islamic times we were worshiping a stone, then we heard a caller calling: O people of the wanderers, indeed your Lord has destroyed you. So seek a Lord. He said: So we went out against every difficulty and humiliation, and while we were still seeking, we found a caller calling out: Indeed. We have found your Lord, or His likeness. He said: Then we came, and behold, a stone, so we sacrificed red stones on it."
34616,"(34616) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Shubail ibn Awf, and he was the most learned of the Jahiliyah."
34617,"(34617) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Raja’, who said: I said to Al-Hasan Al-Basri: When is your promise? In the city? He said: I did not have a period with her after Siffin. He said: I said: When did you have a wet dream? He said: A year after Siffin."
34618,"(34618) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The lifespan of Adam was a thousand years, and the lifespan of David was sixty years, so Adam said: Oh Lord, add forty years to my life, so He completed a thousand years for Adam, and He completed a hundred years for David.
(Ahmed 251. Ibn Saad 28)"
34619,"(34619) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Noah was sent for forty years, and he remained among his people for a thousand years, minus fifty years, to call upon them, and he lived after the flood. Sixty years, until the people became numerous and disobedient. (Hakim 545)"
34620,"(34620) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu"
34621,"(34621) Ismail bin Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Joseph was thrown into the pit when he was seven years old. For ten years, he was in slavery, kingship, and prison for eighty years, then he was reunited, and he lived after that. Twenty-three years."
34622,"(34622) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Razin, who said: It was said to Al-Abbas: Are you older, or the mother of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: He is older than me, and I was born before him."
34623,"(34623) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, he said: It was said to Abu Wa’il: You are Akbar, or Rabi’ Ibn Khuthaym? He said: I am older than him in age, and he is greater in mind than you."
34624,"(34624) Abdă bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Abu continued He was a virgin due to his succession to the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he died when he was sixty-three years old."
34625,"(34625) Ghandar narrated to us, Shu’ba narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I asked Abu Ubaidah: Do you remember a servant? God is something? He said: I do not mention anything about it."
34626,"(34626) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Shuaib bin Al-Habhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: I saw Uthman pouring water on him. Jug"
34627,"(34627) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, and Malik Ibn Mughul, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: He was the first to judge. In Kufa, here is Salman bin Rabi’a Al-Bali. He sat for forty days without an opponent coming to him."
34628,"(34628) Abdul bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God married me. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him when I was six years old, and he built me when I was nine years old. (Bukhari 3894, Muslim 1039)"
34629,"(34629) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: He was between Adam and Noah. Ten of the Qarn, all of them adhered to Islam."
34630,"(34630) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: I heard Al-Hudhali asking Ja’far: How old was Ali when he... Did he die? He said: He was killed when he was fifty-eight, and Al-Hasan died for her, and Al-Hussein was killed for her."
34631,"(34631) Affan told us, he said: Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I heard my father, he said: Abu Uthman told us; Othman was killed in the middle of the days of the Tashreeq."
34632,"(34632) Abu Nu’aym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Ghasil narrated to us, on the authority of Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid said: Ibrahim bin the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died when he was eighteen months old. And he said: He has a wet nurse in Paradise."
34633,"(34633) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: It was me and Al-Aswad bin Yazid was in the police with Amr bin Harith, the nights of Musaab."
34634,"(34634) He told us his youth, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurayh, on the authority of his father; He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he had already visited Aleppo and Syria. (Abu Dawud 1077. Ahmad 19)"
34635,"(34635) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Hanash bin Al-Harith narrated to us, he said: I saw Suwayd bin Ghaflali passing to a woman. He is from Banu Asad, and he is twenty-seven years old."
34636,"(34636) They mentioned that Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari died when he was sixty-three, and he died at the age of forty-four, in the command of Mu’awiyah. May God have mercy on you"
34637,(34637) Al-Abbas died during the rule of Othman.
34638,(34638) Ibn Masoud died during the last period of Uthman’s rule.
34639,(34639) Hudhayfy died when the killing of Uthman came.
34640,(34640) Jabir bin Zayd died.
34641,"(34641) And Anas bin Malik in Jumu’ah, age ninety-three."
34642,(34642) Ibn Umar died at the age of seventy-three.
34643,(34643) And Aisha died.
34644,"(34644) And Al-Hasan bin Ali, fifty-eight years old."
34645,(34645) Amr bin Harith died in the year eighty-five.
34646,"(34446) Al-Hussein bin Ali was killed at the age of sixty-one, on the day of Ashura. Sinan bin Anas Al-Nakha’i killed him. Al-Wahabili, may God curse him, brought his head, Khawli bin Zaid Al-Asbahi, to Ubaid Allah bin Zaid."
34647,(34647) Ibn al-Zubayr was killed at the age of seventy-three.
34648,(34648) Ibn al-Hanafiyyah died at the age of eighty.
34649,(34649) Ibn Abbas died in the year sixty-eight.
34650,(34650) Shuraih died at the age of seventy-three.
34651,(34651) Ali bin Al-Hussein died at the age of ninety-two.
34652,(34652) Abu Ja’far died in the year one hundred and fourteen.
34653,(34653) Saeed bin Al-Musayyab died in the year ninety-three.
34654,(34654) Musa bin Talha died in the year one hundred and six.
34655,(34655) Abu Burda died.
34656,(34656) And Al-Sha’bi in the year one hundred and four.
34657,(34657) Abu Burda died when he was Ibn Naif and eighty years old.
34658,(34658) Saeed bin Jubayr was killed in the year ninety-five.
34659,(34659) Abraham died at the age of ninety-six.
34660,(34660) Omar bin Abdul Aziz died in the year one hundred and one.
34661,(34661) Al-Hasan died.
34662,(34662) And Ibn Sirin in the year one hundred and ten.
34663,(34663) Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d died during the time of Suleiman bin Abdul-Malik.
34664,(34664) Mujahid died in the year one hundred and two.
34665,(34665) Ad-Dahhak died in the year one hundred and five.
34666,(34666) Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi died at the age of one hundred and eight.
34667,(34667) Talha al-Yami died in the year one hundred and twelve.
34668,(34668) Zubaid died in the year one hundred and twenty-two.
34669,(34669) Salamah died in the year one hundred and twenty-first.
34670,(34670) Mansour died in the year one hundred and thirty-two.
34671,(34671) And his leaders died.
34672,"(34672) And Nafi’, in the year one hundred and seventeen."
34673,(34673) Al-Hakam died in the year one hundred and fifteen.
34674,(34674) Abu Qays died.
34675,"(34675) and continuing,"
34676,"(34676) And Hammad, in the year one hundred and twenty."
34677,(34677) Abu Sakhrah died at the age of one hundred and eighteen.
34678,(34678) Habib died in the year one hundred and nineteen.
34679,(34679) Amr bin Murra died in the year one hundred and seventeen.
34680,(34680) Ata’ died in the year one hundred and fifteen.
34681,(34681) And he died in the year one hundred and thirty-six.
34682,(34682) Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman died.
34683,"(34683) And Hisham bin Urwah, in the year one hundred and forty-five."
34684,(34684) Abu Ishaq died.
34685,(34685) And Jabir al-Ju’fi in the year one hundred and twenty-eight.
34686,(34686) Mas’ar died in the year one hundred and fifty-five.
34687,(34687) Ali bin Saleh died in the year one hundred and fifty-four.
34688,(34688) Al-Thawri died in the year one hundred and sixty-one.
34689,(34689) And my people died in the year one hundred and sixty.
34690,"(34690) Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq ruled for two and a half years, and he died during the migration of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the year Twelve"
34691,"(34691) Omar Ibn Al-Khattab ruled for ten and a half years, and he was killed during the age of twenty-three of the Prophet’s migration sites, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, in Dhul-Hijjah."
34692,"(34692) Othman bin Affan ruled for twelve years, and was killed at the age of thirty-five in Dhul-Hijjah."
34693,"(34693) Ali ruled for five years, and in the year forty of the Prophet’s Migrants, may God bless him and grant him peace, he was killed in the month of Ramadan. Ramadan, on the night of the twenty-first of Friday, and he died on the night of Sunday."
34694,"(34694) Mu’awiyah appointed him as governor for twenty years, except for something, and he died at the age of sixty from al-Muhajir."
34695,(34695) Yazid bin Muawiyah ruled for three and a half years.
34696,(34696) Ibn al-Zubayr’s trial lasted nine years.
34697,(34697) Marwan bin Al-Hakam ruled for about nine or ten months.
34698,(34698) Abdul-Malik bin Marwan ruled for fourteen years.
34699,(34699) He was the guardian of the newborn for nine years.
34700,"(34700) And Solomon’s guardian,"
34701,"(34701) and Omar bin Abdul Aziz, each of them two and a half years old."
34702,(34702) Hisham bin Abdul-Malik ruled for twenty years except a few months.
34703,(34703) Al-Walid bin Yazid was the guardian of Al-Walid for about two years.
34704,(34704) And Yazid bin Al-Walid bin Abdul-Malik ruled for six months.
34705,(34705) And Abraham ruled for forty nights.
34706,"(34706) Marwan bin Muhammad bin Marwan ruled for five years, and he is the one from whom the caliphate was taken."
34707,(34707) Abu Abbas appointed Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas as ruler for four and a half years.
34708,"(34708) Abu Ja`far, whose name is Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ali, ruled for twenty-two years."
34709,(34709) The Mahdi ruled for ten years.
34710,(34710) Musa ibn al-Mahdi ruled for years and months.
34711,(34711) Aaron ruled for twenty-three years.
34712,"(34712) Al-Ma’mun ruled for twenty-two years, not including one month."
34713,(34713) Ibn Idris mentioned: He said: I asked Israel: How much did Abu Ishaq Ibn die? He said: He died at the age of ninety-six.
34714,(34714) Al-Sha’bi was two years older than him.
34715,(34715) Talhah was killed
34716,"(34716) And Al-Zubayr was in Rajab, thirty-six years old."
34717,(34717) Masruq died at the age of sixty-three.
34718,(34718) Al-Aswad died in the year seventy-four.
34719,(34719) Ubaidah died at the age of sixty-four.
34720,(34720) Alqamiya bin Qays died in the year sixty-two.
34721,(34721) Amr bin Maymun died in the year seventy-five.
34722,(34722) Abu’un al-Thaqafi died in the year one hundred and fifty-one.
34723,(34723) Malik bin Mughal died in the year one hundred and fifty-one.
34724,(34724) And Israel died in the year one hundred and sixty.
34725,(34725) Qais bin Al-Rabi’ died.
34726,"(34726) And Ja’far al-Ahmar, in the year one hundred and sixty-seven."
34727,(34727) Sharik bin Abdullah died in the year one hundred and seventy-seven.
34728,(34728) Mujahid bin Jabr died in the year one hundred and two.
34729,(34729) Rab’i bin Harash died during the time of Omar bin Abdul Aziz.
34730,(34730) - We have been informed that the name of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq is Abdullah bin Uthman.
